COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[101,"§Firdaus\n‘Firdous’ is one of the names of paradise. The Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ كَانَتْ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتُ الْفِرْدَوْسِ نُزُلًا\nIndeed, those who have believed and done righteous deeds - they will have the Gardens of Paradise (Firdaus) as a lodging.\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-107)\nThe ‘Firdaus’ will be the abode of the people with the following qualities:\n﴿الَّذِينَ هُمْ فِي صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُونَ ٢ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَنِ اللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُونَ ٣ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِلزَّكَاةِ فَاعِلُونَ ٤ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِفُرُوجِهِمْ حَافِظُونَ ٥ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ أَزْوَاجِهِمْ أَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُومِينَ ٦ فَمَنِ ابْتَغَىٰ وَرَاءَ ذَٰلِكَ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْعَادُونَ ٧ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِأَمَانَاتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَاعُونَ ٨ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَلَىٰ صَلَوَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُونَ ٩ أُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُونَ ١٠ الَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ الْفِرْدَوْسَ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ ١١﴾\n1. They who are during their prayer humbly submissive\n2. And they who turn away from ill speech.\n3. And they who are observant of zakah.\n4. And they who guard their private parts. Except from their wives or those their right hands possess, for indeed, they will not be blamed - But whoever seeks beyond that, then those are the transgressors.\n5. And they who are to their trusts and their promises attentive\n6. And they who carefully maintain their prayers –\nThose are the inheritors. Who will inherit al-Firdaus. They will abide therein eternally.\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Mu’minun, Verses-2-11)\n‘Firdaus’ is the highest level of paradise. It is narrated in one sahih hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Paradise has one hundred grades which Allah has reserved for the fighters in His cause, and the distance between each of the two grades is like the distance between the sky and the earth. So when you ask Allah(swt), ask for Al Firdaus, for it is the best and highest part of Paradise. And above it is the throne of Allah(swt) from where the rivers of paradise originate.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 7422)"],[102,"§Fish\nIn the Holy Quran, the word ‘Hut’ has been used for fish. Actually ‘hut’ is used in Arabic for whale and the other fishes are called samak, but in the Holy Quran ‘hut’ has been used for both the whale and other fishes also.\n‘Hut’ is used for a whale:\n﴿وَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٣٩ إِذْ أَبَقَ إِلَى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُونِ ١٤٠ فَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُدْحَضِينَ ١٤١ فَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيمٌ ١٤٢﴾\nAnd indeed, Jonah was among the messengers. [Mention] when he ran away to the laden ship. And he drew lots and was among the losers. Then the fish swallowed him, while he was blameworthy.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-139-142)\nAt another place the Holy Prophet(saws) is being asked to have courage and patience:\nفَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ الْحُوتِ إِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ\nThen be patient for the decision of your Lord, [O Muhammad], and be not like the companion of the fish when he called out while he was distressed.\n(Quran, Surah-68, Al-Qalam, Verse-48)\nIt is being said in the above verse that O Muhammad! Do not be like Yunus who came out of his village before the command of his Lord.\n(For more information see Yunus(as))\n‘Hut’ used for a fish:\nIn the story about Musa(as), the word ‘hut’ is used for some small fish because it is obviously not possible to carry a whale along.\n﴿فَلَمَّا بَلَغَا مَجْمَعَ بَيْنِهِمَا نَسِيَا حُوتَهُمَا فَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيلَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ سَرَبًا ٦١ فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَا قَالَ لِفَتَاهُ آتِنَا غَدَاءَنَا لَقَدْ لَقِينَا مِن سَفَرِنَا هَٰذَا نَصَبًا ٦٢ قَالَ أَرَأَيْتَ إِذْ أَوَيْنَا إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ فَإِنِّي نَسِيتُ الْحُوتَ وَمَا أَنسَانِيهُ إِلَّا الشَّيْطَانُ أَنْ أَذْكُرَهُ ۚ وَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيلَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ عَجَبًا﴾\nBut when they reached the junction between them, they forgot their fish, and it took its course into the sea, slipping away. So when they had passed beyond it, [Moses] said to his boy, \"Bring us our morning meal. We have certainly suffered in this, our journey, [much] fatigue.\" He said, \"Did you see when we retired to the rock? Indeed, I forgot [there] the fish. And none made me forget it except Satan - that I should mention it. And it took its course into the sea amazingly\".\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verses-61-63)\nFish is tasty food which Allah(swt) has created for humans. People have been fishing since ancient times. For the Bani-Israel, Saturday had been declared a day for rest and worship and they were forbidden to do any kind of work or hunting or fishing on that day. But when they became arrogant and started transgressing the limits, they violated the sanctity of that day. Describing this, the Holy Quran says:\nوَاسْأَلْهُمْ عَنِ الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِي كَانَتْ حَاضِرَةَ الْبَحْرِ إِذْ يَعْدُونَ فِي السَّبْتِ إِذْ تَأْتِيهِمْ حِيتَانُهُمْ يَوْمَ سَبْتِهِمْ شُرَّعًا وَيَوْمَ لَا يَسْبِتُونَ ۙ لَا تَأْتِيهِمْ ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَبْلُوهُم بِمَا كَانُوا يَفْسُقُونَ\nAnd ask them about the town that was by the sea - when they transgressed in [the matter of] the sabbath - when their fish came to them openly on their sabbath day, and the day they had no sabbath they did not come to them. Thus did We give them trial because they were defiantly disobedient.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-163)\nTo bypass this restriction, they dug holes near the shore into which the fish would swim on the day of Sabbath. Then when the day was over, they would catch the trapped fish."],[103,"§Frog\nFrog is an animal which lives in water. Among the punishments which Allah(swt) sent to the people of Pharaoh(Firaun), the plague of frogs was one. Egypt was infested with frogs in large numbers. The Holy Quran says:\nفَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الطُّوفَانَ وَالْجَرَادَ وَالْقُمَّلَ وَالضَّفَادِعَ وَالدَّمَ آيَاتٍ مُّفَصَّلَاتٍ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا وَكَانُوا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِينَ\nSo We sent upon them the flood and locusts and lice and frogs and blood as distinct signs, but they were arrogant and were a criminal people.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-133)\nThis punishment of frogs is described in detail in the Bible.\n(See: Bible, Exodus 8:1-14)"],[104,"§Furqan\nThe meaning of ‘Furqan’ is ‘the criterion between right and wrong’. Furqan is one of the names of the Holy Quran. As it says in the Holy Quran itself:\nتَبَارَكَ الَّذِي نَزَّلَ الْفُرْقَانَ عَلَىٰ عَبْدِهِ لِيَكُونَ لِلْعَالَمِينَ نَذِيرًا\nBlessed is He who sent down the Criterion upon His Servant that he may be to the worlds a warner.\n(Quran, Surah-25, Al-Furqan, Verse-1)\nThe twenty-fifth sura of the Holy Quran is ‘Al-Furqan’ which was revealed in Makka and has a total of 77 verses. Among the various qualities of the Holy Quran, one is that it is ‘Furqan’:\nشَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِي أُنزِلَ فِيهِ الْقُرْآنُ هُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ وَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِّنَ الْهُدَىٰ وَالْفُرْقَانِ ۚ\nThe month of Ramadhan [is that] in which was revealed the Qur'an, a guidance for the people and clear proofs of guidance and criterion.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-185)\nIn the same sense it says at another place:\nوَإِذْ آتَيْنَا مُوسَى الْكِتَابَ وَالْفُرْقَانَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ\nAnd [recall] when We gave Moses the Scripture and criterion that perhaps you would be guided.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-53)\nThe meaning of Furqan here is a touchstone with which man can know at every step what is right and what is wrong and which path to follow and which one to stay away from. Which path leads us to Allah(swt) and which to the Satan? That is, this is the wisdom which Allah(swt) grants to His chosen ones namely the rightly-guided. In the same sense the Holy Quran says:\nوَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ الْفُرْقَانَ وَضِيَاءً وَذِكْرًا لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ\nAnd We had already given Moses and Aaron the criterion and a light and a reminder for the righteous.\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verse-48)\nOne other meaning of ‘Furqan’ which occurs in the Holy Quran is ‘day of decision’ as the day of Badr is described in Surah-8, Al-Anfal because this was the day when the two armies met and victory was for the people on the path of Allah(swt). (See Surah-8, Al-Anfal, Verse-41)"],[105,"§Gambling\nGambling is called ‘Maisir’ in Arabic. This means ‘ease’; that is money obtained without any work and without exchanging something. Money is either gained or lost in a short time and it is called a ‘game of chance’.\nGambling has been going on since ancient times. But this is actually taking someone’s wealth without any right. So, Islam has forbidden gambling forever.\nGambling had become a way of life for many people and so the following verse was first revealed:\nيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ ۖ قُلْ فِيهِمَا إِثْمٌ كَبِيرٌ وَمَنَافِعُ لِلنَّاسِ وَإِثْمُهُمَا أَكْبَرُ مِن نَّفْعِهِمَا ۗ\nThey ask you about wine and gambling. Say, \"In them is great sin and [yet, some] benefit for people. But their sin is greater than their benefit.\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-219)\nFrom the above verse the people first realized that drinking and gambling have more harm than benefit. Then the following verse was revealed:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْأَنصَابُ وَالْأَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَاجْتَنِبُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٩٠ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَاءَ فِي الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمْ عَن ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ وَعَنِ الصَّلَاةِ ۖ فَهَلْ أَنتُم مُّنتَهُونَ ٩١﴾\nO you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone alters [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through intoxicants and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-90,91)\nAfter the revelation of these verses the companions understood that now drinking and gambling were haram. After that the scholars also understood it the same way. So, ultimately the Muslim scholars became unanimous in their opinion that both drinking and gambling are haram or forbidden forever. And so the wealth gained from gambling is also forbidden."],[106,"§Gandna(Leek)\nGandna is a type of leafy vegetable which looks like the onion leaves and it is eaten raw in salad form in the Arab countries. It is grown abundantly in the Arab countries and is called ‘Kurrat’. Eating this causes bad breath and hence it is forbidden to enter the mosque after eating it. There is no mention of this in the Holy Quran, but the Sahih Hadith describe it."],[107,"§Garlic\nGarlic is a type of vegetable which is eaten both cooked and raw. Eating it raw causes bad mouth odour; hence it is forbidden to enter the mosque after eating it. See ‘Onion’."],[108,"§Ghaib\nSee ‘Invisible or hidden’."],[109,"§Ghulam\nThe word ‘Ghulam’ is used in the Holy Quran to mean a boy. (See Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-40; Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-19; Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-80, Surah-19, Maryam, Verse-7).\nThe plural of Ghulam is ‘Ghilman’. Among the attractions of the paradise are the ‘Ghilman’ who are boys serving the dwellers of paradise and who would be shining like ‘well-protected pearls’ (See Surah-52, At-Tur, Verse-24)\nIn the Indian languages, ‘Ghulam’ means a ‘slave’ which is ‘Abd’ in Arabic. In the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith, ‘Abd’ is used both for a ‘slave’ and ‘a free person’. For example:\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَآيَةً لِّكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُّنِيبٍ\nIndeed in that is a sign for every servant turning back [to Allah].\n(Quran, Surah-34, Saba, Verse-9)\nIt is said in the case of Nuh(as):\nإِنَّهُ كَانَ عَبْدًا شَكُورًا\nIndeed, he was a grateful servant.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Al-Isra, Verse-3)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) has also been addressed as ‘Abd’ or ‘servant’:\n﴿أَرَأَيْتَ الَّذِي يَنْهَىٰ ٩ عَبْدًا إِذَا صَلَّىٰ ١٠﴾\nHave you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays?\n(Quran, Surah-96, Al-Alaq, Verses-9,10)\nThe person indicated here is the chieftain of the disbelievers, Abu-Lahab who would try to prevent the Holy Prophet(saws) from praying.\nThe other meaning of ‘Abd’ is ‘slave’ or ‘Ghulam’ in the Indian languages. The Holy Quran says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِصَاصُ فِي الْقَتْلَى ۖ الْحُرُّ بِالْحُرِّ وَالْعَبْدُ بِالْعَبْدِ وَالْأُنثَىٰ بِالْأُنثَىٰ ۚ\nO you who have believed, prescribed for you is legal retribution for those murdered - the free for the free, the slave for the slave, and the female for the female.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-178)\nوَلَا تُنكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنُوا ۚ وَلَعَبْدٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَكُمْ\nAnd do not marry polytheistic men [to your women] until they believe. And a believing slave is better than a polytheist, even though he might please you.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-221)\nHere the question arises as to how people became slaves?\nWe come to know from history that the custom of slaves came into existence during the time of Jesus Christ. A few reasons for the beginning of the slave-system are as follows:\nThe poor who were unable to repay their debts would sell off themselves for a given period of time.\nSelling off their children by the poor due to poverty.\nPeople caught stealing would be retained as slaves.\nThe captives of war would be made slaves and be distributed among the victors.\nTraders would capture people of the poorer nations and sell them off to richer nations as in the case of Africans being sold off to Europeans and Americans. Even today the place in Singhal is preserved where the European ships would be harbored to be filled with people chased at gun-point. When the ships were filled to capacity, they would set sail and the people would be sold in the European markets as lifelong slaves.\nThe first three methods have been described in the Bible; but using these methods only the non-Jews were enslaved and not the Jews. (See: Bible, Leviticus 25:39-43 and Exodus 21:7, 22:1-3)\nBut Islam has abolished all these laws and has declared the making of slaves from free people a great sin and also advocates the freeing of slaves in various ways. A few ways which have been described in the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith are as follows:\nIf someone kills a Muslim unintentionally, then in addition to paying the compensation, the culprit is required to free a slave. (Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-92)\nThe compensation for Zihar is the freeing of a slave. (Quran, Surah-58, Al-Mujadla, Verse-3)\nThe compensation for breaking an oath is the freeing of a slave. (Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-89)\nFreeing a slave is a good deed. The Holy Quran has given this the name ‘difficult pass’ or ‘Aqba’ because good deeds are done overcoming the human desires and the Satan is forever trying to confuse us.(Quran, Surah-90, Al-Balad, Verses-11,12)\nDuring the solar and the lunar eclipses, we should free a slave as the Holy Prophet(saws) would do so. (Sahih Bukhari: 2519)\nIf a person frees a Muslim slave, Allah(swt) will free each and every organ of that person from hell-fire. (Sahih Bukhari 2517 and Sahih Muslim 1509)\nIf a person owns a female slave and takes good care of her and then marries her, then he shall be doubly rewarded by Allah(swt). (Sahih Bukhari 2544).\nAccording to the sahih hadith, if a person fasting during Ramadan has intercourse with his wife, then he should free a slave as kaffara.\nThat is, Islam has opened various doors for the freeing of slaves and closed all doors of making slaves. The only way left open is the enslaving of the war captives because other than enslaving them and getting work out of them, there is no other way. But Islam again mentions various ways of freeing these slaves also. A few ways are:\n1. Freeing the non-Muslim soldiers in exchange for Muslim soldiers.\n2. Taking Fidya(compensation) and freeing the slaves.\n3. If they can teach something, freeing them in return for it.\n4. If the ruler wishes, then he should free the slaves.\n5. If somebody embraces Islam of his own free will, then freeing him.\nIf after all this, somebody is made a slave, then we are to treat him very well as is explained below:\nThe male and female slaves should be married to each other (Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-32)\nAs was done in the ancient times, the slave girls should not be forced into prostitution. (Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-33)\nIf they wish to have a contract for eventual emancipation, then they should be given one. (Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-33)\nA female slave should not be separated from her children and if somebody does so, then on the day of Resurrection, he will be separated from his near and dear ones. According to a sahih hadith, Ali(ra) sold off one of the two slave brothers. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know of this, he ordered him to get him back because it would mean a separation between two brothers.\nAccording to another sahih hadith, while partaking the food prepared by a slave, he should also be included in the meal. If the food is very less, a few morsels should at least be given to him. (Sahih Bukhari 2557)\nIn this way Islam gives various rights to the slaves and there is no other religion in history where the slaves are treated in a more humane way."],[110,"§Ghusl\nGhusl means a bath. The description is given in only one place in the Holy Quran:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَقْرَبُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَأَنتُمْ سُكَارَىٰ حَتَّىٰ تَعْلَمُوا مَا تَقُولُونَ وَلَا جُنُبًا إِلَّا عَابِرِي سَبِيلٍ حَتَّىٰ تَغْتَسِلُوا\nO you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying or in a state of janabah, except those passing through [a place of prayer], until you have washed [your whole body].\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-43)\nThat is after intercourse or after contacting any other impurity, it is forbidden to offer salah without ghusl. If water is not available then it is permitted to perform ‘tayammum’ and offer salah. We understand from the sahih hadith that the conditions under which ghusl becomes obligatory are as follows:\nWhen semen comes out either as a result of intercourse or due to a wet dream.\nWhen the male and female private parts come in contact, with or without the semen coming out. According to sahih hadith:\nWhen the male and female private come in contact with each other, then ghusl becomes compulsory.\n(Sahih Muslim, 349)\nAccording to another sahih hadith, whether or not the semen comes out, ghusl is obligatory.\n(Sahih Muslim, 348)\nAt the end of her menses, a woman should cleanse herself, that is perform ghusl. (Sahih Bukhari, 306 and Sahih Muslim, 262)\nWithout ghusl, a woman can neither recite the Holy Quran nor offer salah. Ghusl under some conditions is not obligatory but preferable. For example:\n-ghusl on Friday\n-ghusl on Id days\n-ghusl before donning the ehram\n-ghusl while entering Makka\n-ghusl before the stay in Arafat\n-ghusl before every salah in case of Istihajaa(bleeding even after the end of menses due to some disease during which salah is obligatory)\n-ghusl before accepting Islam\n-ghusl after regaining consciousness after becoming unconscious.\nThe above situations are those in which ghusl is preferable but not compulsory. Some scholars are of the opinion that the Friday ghusl is obligatory."],[111,"§Ginger\nSee ‘Zanjabeel’."],[112,"§Goat\nSince ancient times man has been rearing goats because for one thing it is very easy to take care of them and it gives us many useful things like milk, meat, wool, skin(leather) etc. One popular thing about the prophets is that they reared goats. It says in the Holy Quran about Musa(as), that when he was asked:\n﴿وَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ ١٧ قَالَ هِيَ عَصَايَ أَتَوَكَّأُ عَلَيْهَا وَأَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلَىٰ غَنَمِي وَلِيَ فِيهَا مَآرِبُ أُخْرَىٰ ١٨﴾\nAnd what is that in your right hand, O Moses?\" He said, \"It is my staff; I lean upon it, and I bring down leaves for my sheep and I have therein other uses.\"\n(Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verses-17,18)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) would take the goats of the people of Makka for grazing before his prophethood.\nAmong the animals whose meat Allah(swt) has made halal for eating, the goat is one. That is, an animal belonging to the species of goat, whether male or female can be eaten. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿ثَمَانِيَةَ أَزْوَاجٍ ۖ مِّنَ الضَّأْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَمِنَ الْمَعْزِ اثْنَيْنِ ۗ قُلْ آلذَّكَرَيْنِ حَرَّمَ أَمِ الْأُنثَيَيْنِ أَمَّا اشْتَمَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ أَرْحَامُ الْأُنثَيَيْنِ ۖ نَبِّئُونِي بِعِلْمٍ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ١٤٣ وَمِنَ الْإِبِلِ اثْنَيْنِ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ اثْنَيْنِ ۗ قُلْ آلذَّكَرَيْنِ حَرَّمَ أَمِ الْأُنثَيَيْنِ أَمَّا اشْتَمَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ أَرْحَامُ الْأُنثَيَيْنِ ۖ أَمْ كُنتُمْ شُهَدَاءَ إِذْ وَصَّاكُمُ اللَّهُ بِهَٰذَا ۚ فَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرَىٰ عَلَى اللَّهِ كَذِبًا لِّيُضِلَّ النَّاسَ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ ١٤٤﴾\n[They are] eight mates - of the sheep, two and of the goats, two. Say, \"Is it the two males He has forbidden or the two females or that which the wombs of the two females contain? Inform me with knowledge, if you should be truthful.\" And of the camels, two and of the cattle, two. Say, \"Is it the two males He has forbidden or the two females or that which the wombs of the two females contain? Or were you witnesses when Allah charged you with this? Then who is more unjust than one who invents a lie about Allah to mislead the people by [something] other than knowledge? Indeed, Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.\"\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verses-143,144)\nNow, if someone forbids something for himself, then it is his own mistake. Allah(swt) has not forbidden it for him. In fact Allah(swt) asks those people who have forbidden the meat of the above animals if Allah(swt) has ordered it. Or if they were present when according to them Allah(swt) has forbidden it?\nGoat is one among those eight pairs of animals which can be sacrificed.\nBut for their transgression, Allah(swt) had forbidden the fat of the cattle and sheep for the Jews:\nوَعَلَى الَّذِينَ هَادُوا حَرَّمْنَا كُلَّ ذِي ظُفُرٍ ۖ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ وَالْغَنَمِ حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ شُحُومَهُمَا إِلَّا مَا حَمَلَتْ ظُهُورُهُمَا أَوِ الْحَوَايَا أَوْ مَا اخْتَلَطَ بِعَظْمٍ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ جَزَيْنَاهُم بِبَغْيِهِمْ ۖ وَإِنَّا لَصَادِقُونَ\nAnd to those who are Jews We prohibited every animal of uncloven hoof; and of the cattle and the sheep We prohibited to them their fat, except what adheres to their backs or the entrails or what is joined with bone. [By] that We repaid them for their injustice. And indeed, We are truthful.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-146)"],[113,"§Goliath\n‘Jalut’ or ‘Goliath’ was a Palestinian who was six cubits and a span(about nine feet tall)(See 1 Samuel 17:4). The Palestinians considered him their leader and fought the Bani-Israel under his leadership. His name is mentioned thrice in the Holy Quran:\nFirst: When Talut(Saul) took a test of his army:\nفَلَمَّا فَصَلَ طَالُوتُ بِالْجُنُودِ قَالَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مُبْتَلِيكُم بِنَهَرٍ فَمَن شَرِبَ مِنْهُ فَلَيْسَ مِنِّي وَمَن لَّمْ يَطْعَمْهُ فَإِنَّهُ مِنِّي إِلَّا مَنِ اغْتَرَفَ غُرْفَةً بِيَدِهِ ۚ فَشَرِبُوا مِنْهُ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّنْهُمْ ۚ فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَهُ هُوَ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ قَالُوا لَا طَاقَةَ لَنَا الْيَوْمَ بِجَالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ\nAnd when Saul went forth with the soldiers, he said, \"Indeed, Allah will be testing you with a river. So whoever drinks from it is not of me, and whoever does not taste it is indeed of me, excepting one who takes [from it] in the hollow of his hand.\" But they drank from it, except a [very] few of them. Then when he had crossed it along with those who believed with him, they said, \"There is no power for us today against Goliath and his soldiers.\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-249)\nSecond: Then the few believers who were left with Talut and believed that one day they would meet Allah(swt) met the army of Goliath. When the two armies faced each other, the soldiers of Talut said:\nوَلَمَّا بَرَزُوا لِجَالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ قَالُوا رَبَّنَا أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا وَثَبِّتْ أَقْدَامَنَا وَانصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِينَ\nAnd when they went forth to [face] Goliath and his soldiers, they said, \"Our Lord, pour upon us patience and plant firmly our feet and give us victory over the disbelieving people.\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-250)\nThird: When the armies of Jalut and Talut (Goliath and Saul) were fighting each other, a great warrior Dawood (who later became Dawood(as)) killed Goliath. The Holy Quran says:\nفَهَزَمُوهُم بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَقَتَلَ دَاوُودُ جَالُوتَ\nSo they defeated them by permission of Allah, and David killed Goliath.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-251) (Bible, 1 Samuel, 17:51)\nGoliath wore a coat of armour from head to foot. Dawood(as) hit him on his forehead with three stones due to which he fell down. Then Dawood(as) killed Goliath with his own sword. Seeing their leader killed, the Palestinians panicked and started running away. The army of Saul chased them and killed whoever was captured. In this way the Palestinians were defeated due to the killing of Goliath."],[114,"§Good Behaviour\nSee ‘Quranic teachings about good behavior.’"],[115,"§Good Deeds\nIn the Holy Quran great stress is laid on good deeds and good behavior and both good deeds and good behavior are the secrets of success both in this world and the Hereafter. The Holy Quran says:\nلَن تَنَالُوا الْبِرَّ حَتَّىٰ تُنفِقُوا مِمَّا تُحِبُّونَ ۚ وَمَا تُنفِقُوا مِن شَيْءٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ\nNever will you attain the good [reward] until you spend [in the way of Allah] from that which you love. And whatever you spend - indeed, Allah is Knowing of it.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-92)\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“You will not be a true momin until you wish for your brother what you wish for yourself.”\nThis is the highest level of good deeds and we cannot imagine a better principle for good behavior and good deeds. At another place in the Holy Quran, it says:\nوَتَعَاوَنُوا عَلَى الْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوَىٰ ۖ وَلَا تَعَاوَنُوا عَلَى الْإِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ\nAnd cooperate in righteousness and piety, but do not cooperate in sin and aggression.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-2)\nIt often happens that people advice others about righteousness and piety but do not implement it themselves. These sort of people have been severely criticized:\nأَتَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبِرِّ وَتَنسَوْنَ أَنفُسَكُمْ وَأَنتُمْ تَتْلُونَ الْكِتَابَ ۚ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ\nDo you order righteousness of the people and forget yourselves while you recite the Scripture? Then will you not reason?\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-44)"],[116,"§Guest\nSee ‘Hospitality’."],[117,"§Haakim\nSee ‘Ruler’."],[118,"§Haam\n‘Haam’ is that camel which has made ten she-camels pregnant. This camel would be left free in the name of some god or goddess. They would neither ride it, nor slaughter it, nor eat its flesh. It would freely roam around wherever it pleased. This was one of the blind beliefs of the Arabs before Islam. This has been addressed in the Holy Quran:\nمَا جَعَلَ اللَّهُ مِن بَحِيرَةٍ وَلَا سَائِبَةٍ وَلَا وَصِيلَةٍ وَلَا حَامٍ ۙ وَلَٰكِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يَفْتَرُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ ۖ وَأَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُونَ\nAllah has not appointed [such innovations as] bahirah or sa'ibah or wasilah or ham. But those who disbelieve invent falsehood about Allah, and most of them do not reason.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-103)"],[119,"§Haawiya\n‘Haawiya’ means a deep pit or an abyss. That is the evil-doers will be thrown into an abyss. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَأَمَّا مَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِينُهُ ٨ فَأُمُّهُ هَاوِيَةٌ ٩﴾\nBut as for one whose scales are light, His refuge will be an abyss.\n(Quran, Surah-101, Al-Qari’a, Verses-8,9)\nThe people who are destined to go to hell:\nHypocrites and disbelievers:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ جَامِعُ الْمُنَافِقِينَ وَالْكَافِرِينَ فِي جَهَنَّمَ جَمِيعًا\nIndeed Allah will gather the hypocrites and disbelievers in Hell all together.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-140)\nThose who ascribe partners to Allah(swt):\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ مَعَ اللَّهِ إِلَٰهًا آخَرَ فَتُلْقَىٰ فِي جَهَنَّمَ مَلُومًا مَّدْحُورًا\nAnd, [O mankind], do not make [as equal] with Allah another deity, lest you be thrown into Hell, blamed and banished.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-39)\nThe people who are worshipped other than Allah(swt) will also go to hell:\nإِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ حَصَبُ جَهَنَّمَ أَنتُمْ لَهَا وَارِدُونَ\nIndeed, you [disbelievers] and what you worship other than Allah are the firewood of Hell. You will be coming to [enter] it.\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verse-98)\nThe people who are worshipped will go to hell means the things like the idols etc. and not the pious people whose idols and graves are worshipped. The pious people who are worshipped never invited others to worship them when they were alive. In fact they always preached monotheism. It was after their death that people started worshipping them. On the day of Judgement, these people will clearly say that they never wanted to be worshipped but the foolish people started doing it on their own. The following description about Isa(as) is given in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ اللَّهُ يَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ أَأَنتَ قُلْتَ لِلنَّاسِ اتَّخِذُونِي وَأُمِّيَ إِلَٰهَيْنِ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ مَا يَكُونُ لِي أَنْ أَقُولَ مَا لَيْسَ لِي بِحَقٍّ ۚ إِن كُنتُ قُلْتُهُ فَقَدْ عَلِمْتَهُ ۚ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِي وَلَا أَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِكَ ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوبِ ١١٦ مَا قُلْتُ لَهُمْ إِلَّا مَا أَمَرْتَنِي بِهِ أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبَّكُمْ ۚ وَكُنتُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيدًا مَّا دُمْتُ فِيهِمْ ۖ فَلَمَّا تَوَفَّيْتَنِي كُنتَ أَنتَ الرَّقِيبَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ وَأَنتَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ ١١٧﴾\nAnd [beware the Day] when Allah will say, \"O Jesus, Son of Mary, did you say to the people, 'Take me and my mother as deities besides Allah?'\" He will say, \"Exalted are You! It was not for me to say that to which I have no right. If I had said it, You would have known it. You know what is within myself, and I do not know what is within Yourself. Indeed, it is You who is Knower of the unseen. I said not to them except what You commanded me - to worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord. And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them; but when You took me up, You were the Observer over them, and You are, over all things, Witness.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-116-117)\nHell will have both humans and jinn:\nوَلَقَدْ ذَرَأْنَا لِجَهَنَّمَ كَثِيرًا مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنسِ\nAnd We have certainly created for Hell many of the jinn and mankind.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-179)\nIn this way the Holy Quran contains a detailed description of hell. The gist of it is that whatever man does in this world, its result will be seen in the Hereafter which is the life which begins after death. The people who have done good deeds will have a good life and good reward and the people who have done evil deeds will have a terrible and everlasting torment in hell. This is because it is often the case that the evil doers do not get their just punishment in this world. But in the court of the Almighty(swt), everybody shall get his just reward or punishment. The evil will go to hell and the good will go to paradise when the court of Allah(swt) is established on the Day of Judgement."],[120,"§Hadith\nHadith means the sayings and actions of the Holy Prophet(saws). When the Holy Prophet(saws) did something in front of someone, or said something before someone, or expressed objection to something, then even they come under hadith. In Islamic terminology this is called ‘Taqreer’ that is the Holy Prophet(saws) did not say anything against it.\nHadith is not described in this sense in the Holy Quran, but the words and actions of the Holy Prophet(saws) have been mentioned in different ways. For example:\nوَمَا آتَاكُمُ الرَّسُولُ فَخُذُوهُ وَمَا نَهَاكُمْ عَنْهُ فَانتَهُوا ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقَابِ\nAnd whatever the Messenger has given you - take; and what he has forbidden you - refrain from. And fear Allah; indeed, Allah is severe in penalty.\n(Quran, Surah-59, Al-Hashr, Verse-7)\nIn the same way Allah(swt) commands:\nوَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤْمِنٍ وَلَا مُؤْمِنَةٍ إِذَا قَضَى اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَمْرًا أَن يَكُونَ لَهُمُ الْخِيَرَةُ مِنْ أَمْرِهِمْ ۗ وَمَن يَعْصِ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلَالًا مُّبِينًا\nIt is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decided a matter, that they should [thereafter] have any choice about their affair. And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly strayed into clear error.\n(Quran, Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verse-36)\nAt one place, the people who disobey the Holy Prophet(saws) have been warned:\nلَّا تَجْعَلُوا دُعَاءَ الرَّسُولِ بَيْنَكُمْ كَدُعَاءِ بَعْضِكُم بَعْضًا ۚ قَدْ يَعْلَمُ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ يَتَسَلَّلُونَ مِنكُمْ لِوَاذًا ۚ فَلْيَحْذَرِ الَّذِينَ يُخَالِفُونَ عَنْ أَمْرِهِ أَن تُصِيبَهُمْ فِتْنَةٌ أَوْ يُصِيبَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ\nDo not make [your] calling of the Messenger among yourselves as the call of one of you to another. Already Allah knows those of you who slip away, concealed by others. So let those beware who dissent from the Prophet's order, lest fitnah strike them or a painful punishment.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-63)\nHadith have very great importance in Islam. There are two basic sources in Islam; namely the Holy Quran and the hadith. It is because of this that right from the beginning, Islamic scholars were continuously engaged in collecting the hadith. These scholars of hadith are called ‘Muhaddis’. For the research and study of hadith, these scholars have formulated certain rules so that the sahih and zaeef hadith can be easily distinguished. For example the sahih hadith have to fulfill the following conditions:\nThe ‘sanad’ or ‘chain of narrators’ should be continuous; that is there should be no narrator who has not heard the hadith directly from the previous narrator in the chain.\nEvery narrator of the chain should be ‘adil’; that is truthful and reliable.\nEvery narrator of the chain should have a good memory.\nThe hadith should not be ‘shaaz’; that is it should not go against a more ‘adil’(reliable) narrator at any point in the chain of narrators.\nAny hadith whose ‘chain of narrators’ or ‘sanad’ fulfills all the above conditions will be termed ‘sahih’ and any hadith whose ‘sanad’ does not fulfill even one condition will be termed ‘zaeef’. Many books have been written about this. The main books of hadith are:\nSahih Bukhari: The author is Imam Abu-Abdullah-Muhammad bin Ismail Bukhari who was born in 194 A.H and died in 256 A.H. All the hadith in this book are ‘sahih’. The total number of hadith in this book without repetition are 2602 and with repetition they are 9082 as mentioned by the famous commentator Hafiz Ibn-Hajar in his book ‘Fath-ul-Baari’.\nSahih Muslim: The author is Imam Muslim-bin-Al-Hajjaj Neshapuri who was born in Neshapur in 204 A.H and died in 261 A.H. All the hadith in this book are sahih whose total without repetition comes to 3033 and with repetition the total is 7390 as mentioned by Mashhoor-bin-Hasan in his book ‘Imam Muslim and his book sahih Muslim’.\nSunan Abu Dawood: The author is Imam Abu-Dawood who was born in 202 A.H. and died in 275 A.H. This book has a total of 4080 hadith but all are not sahih.\nSunan Tirmizi: The author is Abu-Isa Muhammad-bin-Isa Tirmizi who was born in 209 A.H and died in 279 A.H. The total number of hadith are 3956, but all of them are not sahih.\nSunan Nasai: The author is Imam Nasai who was born in 215 A.H and died in 303 A.H. The total number of hadith are 5758, but all of them are not sahih.\nSunan Ibn-Maaja: The author is Imam Ibn-Maaja who was born in 209 A.H and died in 273 A.H. The total number of hadith are 4341, but all of them are not sahih.\nSo, the hadith scholar Shaikh Albani has divided the last four books into two parts each:\nOne sahih and the other zaeef; that is Sahih Abu-Dawood and Zaeef Abu-Dawood; Sahih Tirmizi and Zaeef Tirmizi; Sahih Nasai and Zaeef Nasai; Sahih Ibn-Maaja and Zaeef Ibn-Maaja.\nThe above six books are called ‘Sihah Sitta’ which means ‘six true books’. This does not mean that whatever is written in these books is sahih. But as mentioned earlier, with the exception of Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, the remaining four contain some zaeef hadith also. So, the meaning of ‘Sihah Sitta’ is that the hadith in these books are mainly sahih. One other popular book of hadith is ‘Musnad Imam Ahmad’ whose author is Imam Ahmad-bin-Hambal who was born in 164 A.H and died in 241 A.H. This book contains 24647 hadith which after new research has been published in fifty parts. The last five parts are the index.\nIt is impossible to count the exact number of books of hadith. So, it is helpful to go through the book ‘Arresaala Mustatarfa’ by Kattani(expired in 1345 A.H.)\nIn my opinion, the number of sahih hadith is around fifteen thousand."],[121,"§Haiz\nSee ‘menses’."],[122,"§Hajj\nThe meaning of Hajj is to express one’s wish; that is, it is a form of worship in which the journey is undertaken with the wish to see the Holy Kaaba.\nThe command to perform Hajj:\nHajj is obligatory once in a lifetime upon every man and woman who is in a position to go to the Holy Kaaba; that is after fulfilling the needs of self and family if enough money is left to go to Makka. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلِلَّهِ عَلَى النَّاسِ حِجُّ الْبَيْتِ مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيلًا ۚ\nAnd [due] to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-97)\nIt is specified ‘once in a lifetime’ because it is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“O people, Allah has enjoined Hajj upon you so perform Hajj.” A man asked: “Is it every year, O Messenger of Allah (sallallahu alaihi wa-sallam)?” He (sallallahu alaihi wa-sallam) remained silent until the man had said it three times, then he responded saying: “If I had said yes, (then) it would have become an obligation (once every year) and you would not have been able to do it.” Then he said: “Do not push me to tell you more than what I have left you with, for those who came before you were destroyed because they asked too many questions and argued with their Prophets. If I command you to do a thing, do as much of it as you can, and if I forbid you to do something, then avoid it.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 1337 and Sahih Bukhari, 7288)\nIn this hadith one important principle of Islam is highlighted; that is whatever has been commanded we should do to the best of our capacity(except for the ‘waajib’ things which are compulsory); but the things which have been forbidden we should avoid.\nNow let us see how the Hajj is performed:\nMaking the intention(Niyyah): ‘Niyyah’ is a word in the Islamic terminology which means intention. Whenever a person wishes to perform some act of worship, he makes the intention in his heart that he is doing this for Allah(swt) alone. With this intention, the person dons the ‘ihram’. Four places have been designated as ‘meeqat’ for entering Makka. Whenever the meeqat or the equivalent place arrives, the intention has to be made and the ‘ihram’ donned. ‘Ihram’ can be donned from home itself.\nBefore donning the ‘ihram’, ghusl is performed, nails are cut, the hair of the private parts and arm-pits is removed and preferably fragrance applied.\nAfter reaching Makka, the circumambulation of the Holy Kaaba is done and if the intention is ‘Hajj-e-Tamatto’ then the seven rounds between Safa and Marwa should be completed(Sa’ee). Then the hair of the head is either cut or shaved and the ‘ihram’ is changed and normal clothes are worn. If the intention is for ‘Hajj-e-Qiraan’ or ‘Hajj-e-Ifraad’, then after the circumambulation of the Holy Kaaba, the person remains in his ‘ihram’.\n‘Ihram’ is donned again on the eighth day of Zilhijja (in case they have come out of ‘ihram’) and in this state, the person goes to Mina. Then the person offers the Zuhr, Asr, Magrib, Isha salah of that day and the Fajr prayer of the next day.\nOn the ninth day of Zilhijja, after sun-rise, the person sets out for Arafat and after resting there for some time listens to the sermon of the Imam if possible. Then the Zuhr and Asr salah are combined and if possible offered in Masjid-e-Namira. The prayers can be offered in the tent itself and after that the person engages in earnest supplications to the Almighty(swt) till sun-set because this day of Arafat is extremely important and has great benefits. It is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“There is no day on which Allah frees more people from the Fire than the day of Arafat. He comes close and expresses His pride to the angels saying, ‘What do these people want?’” [Saheeh Muslim, 1348]\nIt is narrated in some hadith that Allah(swt) declares with the angels as witnesses, “Today I have forgiven all these people.”\nThe day of Arafat is the most important day of Hajj. That is why the Hajis fervently supplicate to Almighty(swt) from mid-day to sun-set, seek His forgiveness for their sins and make a commitment not to sin in future. Therefore the true Hajj is that about which the Holy Prophet(saws) says:\n“Whoever performs Hajj for the pleasure of Allah(swt) and does not do evil or sins; then he will return from Hajj free from sins as if he were born anew.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1521 and Muslim, 1350)\nIt means that all his sins are forgiven. The importance of Arafat is narrated in another hadith:\n“Hajj is Arafat.”\nThat is without spending some time in Arafat, Hajj is not complete and that time is from the morning of 9 Zilhijja to the morning of 10 Zilhijja. In these twenty-four hours, if a person stays for some time at least in Arafat, then his Hajj is complete and if someone is unable to reach Arafat, then his Hajj is incomplete.\nArafat is the main place for supplicating to Allah(swt) and therefore the Hajis should engage as much as possible in supplications. They should pray for themselves, their children, their relatives, all the Muslims and for peace in this world etc. because on this day Allah(swt) accepts the prayers of His slaves and grants their wishes in His own way.\nAfter sun-set, the Hajis leave Arafat without offering the Magrib salah and go towards Muzdalifa. The Magrib and Isha prayers are offered together in Muzdalifa.\nIf accompanied by children and weak ladies, after midnight the Hajis set out for Mina.\nIf not accompanied by children and ladies, the Hajis should stay in Muzdalifa till dawn. After offering the Fajr salah, the Hajis supplicate to Allah(swt) which is described in the Holy Quran:\nفَإِذَا أَفَضْتُم مِّنْ عَرَفَاتٍ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ عِندَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ ۖ وَاذْكُرُوهُ كَمَا هَدَاكُمْ وَإِن كُنتُم مِّن قَبْلِهِ لَمِنَ الضَّالِّينَ\nBut when you depart from 'Arafat, remember Allah at al- Mash'ar al-Haram. And remember Him, as He has guided you, for indeed, you were before that among those astray.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-198)\nMash'ar al-Haram is also called Muzdalifa. And at the place where the Holy Prophet(saws) rested, there stands a beautiful mosque.\nAfter spending the night in Muzdalifa, offering the Fajr salah and then supplicating to Allah(swt), on 10 Zilhijja the Hajis set out for Mina where first the Jamarah named ‘Aqba’ is stoned with seven pebbles.\nIf sacrifice is to be done, then the animal is sacrificed.\nThe hair of the head is either shaved or cut and then the Hajis have a bath as is described in the Holy Quran:\nثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ\nThen let them end their untidiness.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-29)\nThat is change from the ‘ihram’ to ordinary clothes. Now, the restrictions of ‘ihram’ no longer bind him. The only thing forbidden now is having intercourse with his wife.\nOn 10 Zilhijja or till 13 Zilhijja, go to Makka for performing the Tawaf-e-Ifaza which is also called Tawaf-e-Ziyarat or Tawaf-e-Haj. Without this ‘tawaf’ or circumambulation the Hajj is incomplete. Then offer two rakat salah.\nThis is the tawaf which is meant in the following verse of the Holy Quran:\nثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْيُوفُوا نُذُورَهُمْ وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ\nThen let them end their untidiness and fulfill their vows and perform Tawaf around the ancient House.\"\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-29)\nThen do the seven rounds between Safa and Marwa(Sa’ee), starting from Safa and ending at Marwa as is explained in the Holy Quran:\nإِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِن شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ ۖ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ أَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَن يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا ۚ\nIndeed, as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever makes Hajj to the House or performs 'umrah - there is no blame upon him for walking between them.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-158)\nThe Sa’ee between Safa and Marwa is a compulsory act of Hajj, but from the above verse ‘there is no blame upon him for walking between them’ had been understood by some companions to mean that Sa’ee is not obligatory. When Aisha(ra) came to know of this she said that if that was the case Allah(swt) would have said, ”If you do not do tawaf between them then it is not wrong.”\nThen it was explained that before embracing Islam, the Ansar would do the Hajj of an idol named ‘Manaat’. After becoming Muslims, when they hesitated to perform the Sa’ee between Safa and Marwa, and said to the Holy Prophet(saws), ”We are hesitating to perform the Sa’ee between Safa and Marwa.” Then Allah(swt) revealed this verse. (See Sahih Bukhari, 1643 and Muslim, 1278)\nIt is narrated in another Sahih hadith of Muslim that before Islam, the Ansar performed the Hajj of two idols named ‘Isaaf’ and ‘Naila’ and then did the Sa’ee of Safa and Marwa. After embracing Islam when they were hesitating to perform the Sa’ee, then this verse was revealed. (See: Muslim, 1277)\nThat is why Sa’ee is a compulsory act of Hajj and after Sa’ee, the Hajj is complete.\n11, 12 and 13 Zilhijja nights have to be spent in Mina. If someone plans to return on the 12th itself, then it is allowed to do so as Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nوَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ فِي أَيَّامٍ مَّعْدُودَاتٍ ۚ فَمَن تَعَجَّلَ فِي يَوْمَيْنِ فَلَا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ وَمَن تَأَخَّرَ فَلَا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ ۚ لِمَنِ اتَّقَىٰ\nAnd remember Allah during [specific] numbered days. Then whoever hastens [his departure] in two days - there is no sin upon him; and whoever delays [until the third] - there is no sin upon him - for him who fears Allah.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-203)\nIn these three days at Mina, the haji has to stone the three jamarahs with seven pebbles each - first the small jamarah, then the middle jamarah and then the big jamarah. This can be done from the dawn of one day to the dawn of the next as given in the fatwa by the highest mufti of Saudi Arabia.\nThe remaining time has to be spent in the remembrance of Allah(swt) as explained in the Holy Quran:\nفَإِذَا قَضَيْتُم مَّنَاسِكَكُمْ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَذِكْرِكُمْ آبَاءَكُمْ أَوْ أَشَدَّ ذِكْرًا\nAnd when you have completed your rites, remember Allah like your [previous] remembrance of your fathers or with [much] greater remembrance.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-200)\nIt is mentioned by Ibn-e-Abbas and the other companions that after their Hajj, the people would assemble in their tents and narrate the stories of their forefathers; their courage, their charity, their bravery etc. Allah(swt) has commanded the Muslims that instead of these ancient stories they should spend their time in the remembrance of Allah(swt) and ask for favors both in this world and the Hereafter lest they ask for the good in this world and forget all about Hereafter. Explaining this in the Holy Quran, Allah(swt) says:\n﴿فَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَمَا لَهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلَاقٍ ٢٠٠ وَمِنْهُم مَّن يَقُولُ رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ ٢٠١ أُولَٰئِكَ لَهُمْ نَصِيبٌ مِّمَّا كَسَبُوا ۚ وَاللَّهُ سَرِيعُ الْحِسَابِ ٢٠٢﴾\nAnd among the people is he who says, \"Our Lord, give us in this world,\" and he will have in the Hereafter no share. But among them is he who says, \"Our Lord, give us in this world [that which is] good and in the Hereafter [that which is] good and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.\" Those will have a share of what they have earned, and Allah is swift in account.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verses-200-202)\nSupplications are very important and the Holy Prophet would supplicate as follows:\n“O Rab! Give us good in this world and also in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of hell-fire.”\n(See Bukhari 4522 and Muslim 2690)\nIn fact it is narrated in Sahih Muslim that the Holy Prophet(saws) would mostly recite this supplication.\nOnce the Holy Prophet(saws) went to see a person who was sick. He saw that the person was reduced to skin and bones due to illness. The Holy Prophet(saws) asked him, “Didn’t you ever supplicate to Allah(swt)?” The person replied, “Yes, I always prayed that O Allah(swt)! Give me the punishment which you intend to give in the Hereafter in this world itself.”\nUpon this the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Allah(swt) is Majestic(SubhanAllah). You do not have His power. Why did you not pray that O Allah(swt)! Give me good in this world and also in the Hereafter and save me from the torment of hell.”\n(See: Muslim, 2688)\nAfter making the intention for Hajj and donning the ‘ihram’, the following restrictions become applicable to him:\nThe men cannot wear any stitched clothes. Women can wear stitched clothes.\nFragrance should not be used.\nHair either from the head or any other part of the body should not be cut.\nThe head should not be covered in case of men.\nMarriage is forbidden in this state.\nIntercourse is forbidden.\nHunting is forbidden.\nIf a haji commits a mistake and does something which is forbidden, then he will have to pay the compensation which is as follows:\nCompensation for cutting the hair or nails, wearing stitched clothing(in case of men), using fragrance or covering the head(in case of men) is:\n1. Fasting for three days.\n2. Or feeding six needy people.\n3. Sacrifice a sheep and distribute it among the poor without eating it himself.\nIf the haji has killed an animal, then an animal which is equal to it has to be sacrificed. If such an animal cannot be found then two people should fix the value of that animal and with that amount the poor people have to be fed or the person should fast. Having intercourse with his wife spoils the Hajj. So, it becomes obligatory that he sacrifices a camel and performs the Hajj the following year. But if someone has intercourse after reaching Mina, stoning the jamarah, offering the sacrifice and shaving the head, then the Hajj is not spoiled and he should simply sacrifice a sheep.\nAfter doing the above things a haji comes out of his ‘ihram’. This is called the first ‘Tahallul’. On completing the Tawaf-e-Ifaza’, it is called the second ‘Tahallul’ and the haji becomes free from all restrictions.\nWhat is Hajj?\nHajj is a kind of international gathering in which all the people of the world assemble to worship one Allah(swt). We learn the following from Hajj:\nFrom every corner of the world the Muslims converge at Makka to worship the one Allah(swt).\nAll are dressed alike, that is two unstitched pieces of cloth, one round the waist and one over the shoulders. The similarity of dress wipes out all distinctions. The rich and the poor, the white and the black – all are the same as Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nيَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنَّا خَلَقْنَاكُم مِّن ذَكَرٍ وَأُنثَىٰ وَجَعَلْنَاكُمْ شُعُوبًا وَقَبَائِلَ لِتَعَارَفُوا\nO mankind, indeed We have created you from male and female and made you peoples and tribes that you may know one another.\n(Quran, Surah-49, Al-Hujurat, Verse-13)\nThat is, all humans are the offspring of one mother and father. One can understand this fact easily during Hajj. All the Muslims performing Hajj dress alike and saying “Allahumma Labbayak”, complete the Hajj helping out each other.\nThe satan moves in the veins of humans along with his blood and Hajj is an excellent way to get rid of him because by stoning the jamarah from the 10th to the 13th of Zilhijja, man is actually killing the satan inside him. In this way the satan who is leading us astray will be expelled from our system forever.\nAccording to the historical records, when Ibraheem(as) was going to sacrifice his son Ismael(as), the satan tried to lead him astray at three places where Ibraheem(as) stoned him and fulfilled his duty.\nIn the six days of Hajj; from the 8th to the 13th, man tries to conquer his senses. This is a kind of test. If man succeeds in this, then he will succeed in his life also. That is, he will carry out the commands of Allah(swt) and control himself from doing the forbidden things. This is indeed a great success in the case of people who experience a great change in themselves after the Hajj:\n﴿وَأَذِّن فِي النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ يَأْتُوكَ رِجَالًا وَعَلَىٰ كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ يَأْتِينَ مِن كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيقٍ ٢٧ لِّيَشْهَدُوا مَنَافِعَ لَهُمْ وَيَذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللَّهِ فِي أَيَّامٍ مَّعْلُومَاتٍ عَلَىٰ مَا رَزَقَهُم مِّن بَهِيمَةِ الْأَنْعَامِ ۖ فَكُلُوا مِنْهَا وَأَطْعِمُوا الْبَائِسَ الْفَقِيرَ ٢٨﴾\nAnd proclaim to the people the Hajj [pilgrimage]; they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel; they will come from every distant pass - That they may witness benefits for themselves and mention the name of Allah on known days over what He has provided for them of [sacrificial] animals. So eat of them and feed the miserable and poor.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-27,28)\nWe have mentioned here a few benefits of Hajj. These benefits of the Hajis are both for this world and the Hereafter."],[123,"§Halal and Haraam\nIn Islam, the right to declare something ‘halal’ or ‘haraam’ is with Almighty Allah(swt) and His(swt) Holy Prophet(saws). That is why the people who issue fatwas about ‘halal’ or ‘haraam’ without adequate knowledge have been severely criticized:\nوَلَا تَقُولُوا لِمَا تَصِفُ أَلْسِنَتُكُمُ الْكَذِبَ هَٰذَا حَلَالٌ وَهَٰذَا حَرَامٌ لِّتَفْتَرُوا عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ ۚ إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَفْتَرُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ لَا يُفْلِحُونَ\nAnd do not say about what your tongues assert of untruth, \"This is lawful and this is unlawful,\" to invent falsehood about Allah. Indeed, those who invent falsehood about Allah will not succeed.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-116)\nThe polytheists had forbidden some things for themselves like the animals set free in the name of some god or goddess. Referring to this, Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nقُلْ أَرَأَيْتُم مَّا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ لَكُم مِّن رِّزْقٍ فَجَعَلْتُم مِّنْهُ حَرَامًا وَحَلَالًا قُلْ آللَّهُ أَذِنَ لَكُمْ ۖ أَمْ عَلَى اللَّهِ تَفْتَرُونَ\nSay, \"Have you seen what Allah has sent down to you of provision of which you have made [some] lawful and [some] unlawful?\" Say, \"Has Allah permitted you [to do so], or do you invent [something] about Allah?\"\n(Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-59)\nIn the same way, addressing the believers, Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تُحَرِّمُوا طَيِّبَاتِ مَا أَحَلَّ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ وَلَا تَعْتَدُوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِينَ\nO you who have believed, do not prohibit the good things which Allah has made lawful to you and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not like transgressors.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-87)\nالَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ الرَّسُولَ النَّبِيَّ الْأُمِّيَّ الَّذِي يَجِدُونَهُ مَكْتُوبًا عِندَهُمْ فِي التَّوْرَاةِ وَالْإِنجِيلِ يَأْمُرُهُم بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَاهُمْ عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ وَيُحِلُّ لَهُمُ الطَّيِّبَاتِ وَيُحَرِّمُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْخَبَائِثَ وَيَضَعُ عَنْهُمْ إِصْرَهُمْ وَالْأَغْلَالَ الَّتِي كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ\nThose who follow the Messenger, the unlettered prophet, whom they find written in what they have of the Torah and the Gospel, who enjoins upon them what is right and forbids them what is wrong and makes lawful for them the good things and prohibits for them the evil and relieves them of their burden and the shackles which were upon them.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-157)\nAt one place, the Holy Prophet(saws) is also addressed:\nيَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ لِمَ تُحَرِّمُ مَا أَحَلَّ اللَّهُ لَكَ ۖ تَبْتَغِي مَرْضَاتَ أَزْوَاجِكَ ۚ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ\nO Prophet, why do you prohibit [yourself from] what Allah has made lawful for you, seeking the approval of your wives? And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\n(Quran, Surah-66, At-Tahrim, Verse-1)\nWe come to know from this that what Allah(swt) declares as ‘halal’, even the Holy Prophet(saws) does not have the authority to declare it ‘haraam’. Other than the Holy Quran, we come to know what is ‘halal’ or ‘haraam’ from the sahih hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws) because the Prophet(saws) has not declared them as such of his own free will but only upon the command of Allah(swt).\nIt is corroborated from one hadith in which the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n”A time will soon come when a man will be reclining on his pillow, and when one of my statements (ahadith) is related to him, he will say: ‘The Book of Allah is (sufficient) between us and you, whatever we find in it being permissible we will take as permissible, and whatever we find in it being forbidden we will take as forbidden.’ But verily, whatever the Messenger of Allah has forbidden is like that which Allah has forbidden.”\n(See: Tirmizi and Ibn-Maaja, 12)\nA few examples also have been given in Abu Dawood 3804; Musnad Ahmad 4:130 etc. For example, it has been said:\n“Be warned that the domestic donkey is not halal. In this way a few other animals are also not halal. In the same way an object which is dropped by a Mu’aahid(non-Muslim messenger who goes with a message to a Muslim state) is also not halal. That is, it has to be returned.”\nIn conclusion we can say that the Holy Prophet(saws) has left behind two things for us. One is the Holy Quran and the other is his sunnah. Whatever is ‘halal’ according to these two is halal(allowed) and whatever is haraam according to them is haraam(forbidden). And absolutely nobody has any authority to declare something which is halal according to these as haraam and something which is haraam according to these as halal. And as long as the Muslims hold on to the Holy Quran and the Sunnah firmly, they shall not be led astray."],[124,"§Hamaan\nHamaan was the minister of the Pharaoh(Firaun). When Allah(swt) sent Musa(as) to the Pharaoh(Firaun), this minister along with the Pharaoh(Firaun) fought Musa(as). Once the Pharaoh(Firaun) ordered him to build a tall tower, climbing which he could search for Allah(swt) who had sent Musa(as):\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ مَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرِي فَأَوْقِدْ لِي يَا هَامَانُ عَلَى الطِّينِ فَاجْعَل لِّي صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّي أَطَّلِعُ إِلَىٰ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ وَإِنِّي لَأَظُنُّهُ مِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ\nAnd Pharaoh said, \"O eminent ones, I have not known you to have a god other than me. Then ignite for me, O Haman, [a fire] upon the clay and make for me a tower that I may look at the God of Moses. And indeed, I do think he is among the liars.\"\n(Quran, Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verse-38)\n﴿وَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يَا هَامَانُ ابْنِ لِي صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّي أَبْلُغُ الْأَسْبَابَ ٣٦ أَسْبَابَ السَّمَاوَاتِ فَأَطَّلِعَ إِلَىٰ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ وَإِنِّي لَأَظُنُّهُ كَاذِبًا ۚ﴾\nAnd Pharaoh said, \"O Haman, construct for me a tower that I might reach the ways - The ways into the heavens - so that I may look at the deity of Moses; but indeed, I think he is a liar.\"\n(Quran, Surah-40, Al-Momin, Verses-36,37)\nThis is the foolishness of the misled people which has not changed since three thousand years because even today we keep getting news that such and such a person has gone into space in search of Allah(swt). But he could not find Him(swt). Especially the communist leaders and the atheist scientists. But who can explain to these fools that the Allah(swt) towards Whom Musa(as) and the other prophets had invited humanity was not somebody with the physical attributes which we can comprehend but Somebody Whom we shall see InshaAllah in the Hereafter. He(swt) is so Majestic that we cannot see Him(swt) with our eyes.(See: Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-103)\nNone of the plans of the Pharaoh(Firaun) and Hamaan were to succeed and neither did they. Musa(as) whom they considered as their worst enemy was brought up in the palace of Pharaoh(Firaun) itself. The Pharaoh(Firaun), his minister Hamaan and their entire army were utterly unsuccessful in suppressing the call of Musa(as).(See: Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verse-8)\nSome European scholars expressed the doubt that the Hamaan described in the Taurah was the minister of an Iranian king who ruled long after the time of Musa(as). He convinced the king to issue an order to kill all the Iranian Jews. But a Jew named Mordecai with the help of a woman named Esther, made the king revoke the order and got an order issued for the killing of Hamaan. In the seventeenth book of the Bible ‘Esther’, this is described in great detail. Now how do we know that there was no minister in the court of Pharaoh(Firaun) with the name Hamaan? Do we have a list of the names of all the ministers and is the name Hamaan missing from it? When it is not so, then there is no cause for doubt. Hamaan has been described in more than one place in the Holy Quran and it is corroborated in the sahih hadith also as is narrated by Abdullah-bin-Amr that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“He who preserves these salahs, will find them to be a light for him, an evidence and a deliverance on the day of resurrection. But, he who does not preserve them will not have them as a light, an evidence and a deliverance, and, on the day of resurrection, he will be with Qaroon, Pharaoh(Firaun), Haman and Ubayy-bin-Kab.\"\n(Musnad Ahmad, 2:169, Daarmi, 2:301)\nAmon is the name of a popular deity of Egypt. Therefore it is not surprising that some priest of this deity was named Hamaan because both the words are quite similar sounding. Or maybe some minister was named after Amon and in the Arabic language it became Hamaan."],[125,"§Ha-Meem\nSee ‘Alif-Laam-Meem’."],[126,"§Hammalatal-Hatab\nThe meaning of Hammalatal-Hatab is the one who carries fuel on her head. The person indicated is the wife of Abu-Lahab who like her husband was a disbeliever. Whenever possible she tried to harm the Holy Prophet(saws). About her Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَامْرَأَتُهُ حَمَّالَةَ الْحَطَبِ ٤ فِي جِيدِهَا حَبْلٌ مِّن مَّسَدٍ ٥﴾\nAnd his wife [as well] - the carrier of firewood. Around her neck is a rope of [twisted] fiber.\n(Quran, Surah-111, Al-Lahab, Verses-4,5)\nHer name was Arwa-bint-Harab. Her father Harab-bin-Umayya and brother Abu-Sufyan-bin-Harab were among the chieftains of Makka. She always wore a crown on her head and a necklace of pearls around her neck. It is said about her that on the day of Resurrection, she will be carrying fuel on her head and round her neck there will be a rope and in this state she will enter hell along with her husband Abu-Lahab. This verse was a prophecy that both of them will not embrace Islam and that they would die in this state and it came true.\nAccording to some historical books it appears that even in this world she died a tragic death. She was collecting some thorny sticks from the mountains to throw in the path of the Holy Prophet(saws), when the rope from the bundle fell round her neck and she was strangled to death.\nThis was the evil end of that evil woman who had gone so far in opposing Islam that she would strew thorns in the path of the Holy Prophet(saws)."],[127,"§Haroon(as)\nIn the Holy Quran two people named Haroon are described. One is the brother of Musa(as) who was made a prophet by Allah(swt) and sent along with Musa(as) to the Pharaoh(Firaun). The other is the brother of Maryam. Firstly Haroon(as), the brother of Musa(as) is being described.\nHe was three years elder to Musa(as). Now the question arises as to why the Pharaoh(Firaun) did not have him killed because he was killing all the boys of Bani-Israel. It is possible that the order was given after the birth of Haroon(as). According to some historians when Pharaoh(Firaun) issued the order to kill all the boys being born, the Egyptians were worried that in that case no men would be left to serve them and till their fields. So, they requested the Pharaoh(Firaun) that the boys be left alone one year and killed the next year. Pharaoh(Firaun) agreed to their request. It is possible that Haroon was born in the year when the boys were not killed. We do not come to know about the childhood of Haroon either from the Holy Quran or the Taurah.\nThe first mention of Haroon is when Allah(swt) made Musa(as) a prophet and sent him to the Pharaoh(Firaun) and his people. Then Musa(as) said:\n﴿قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي قَتَلْتُ مِنْهُمْ نَفْسًا فَأَخَافُ أَن يَقْتُلُونِ ٣٣ وَأَخِي هَارُونُ هُوَ أَفْصَحُ مِنِّي لِسَانًا فَأَرْسِلْهُ مَعِيَ رِدْءًا يُصَدِّقُنِي ۖ إِنِّي أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ ٣٤﴾\nHe said, \"My Lord, indeed, I killed from among them someone, and I fear they will kill me. And my brother Aaron is more fluent than me in tongue, so send him with me as support, verifying me. Indeed, I fear that they will deny me.\"\n(Quran, Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verses-33,34)\nAt another place it says:\n﴿قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ ١٢ وَيَضِيقُ صَدْرِي وَلَا يَنطَلِقُ لِسَانِي فَأَرْسِلْ إِلَىٰ هَارُونَ ١٣﴾\nHe said, \"My Lord, indeed I fear that they will deny me .And that my breast will tighten and my tongue will not be fluent, so send for Aaron.\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verses-12,13)\nAllah(swt) commanded both the brothers to go to Pharaoh(Firaun). The detailed description is given in the Taurah. (See Exodus, 4:10-15). Then both of them went to Pharaoh(Firaun). But as feared by Musa(as), they were rejected and the people said:\nفَقَالُوا أَنُؤْمِنُ لِبَشَرَيْنِ مِثْلِنَا وَقَوْمُهُمَا لَنَا عَابِدُونَ\nThey said, \"Should we believe two men like ourselves while their people are for us in servitude?\"\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Mu’minun, Verse-47)\nHaroon(as) is mentioned again when the magicians of Egypt shout out:\n﴿قَالُوا آمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٤٧ رَبِّ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ ٤٨﴾\nThey said, \"We have believed in the Lord of the worlds, The Lord of Moses and Aaron.\"\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verses-47,48)\nThen the third description occurs in the Holy Quran and the Taurah when Musa(as) goes to Mount Tur to get the Taurah and leaves behind Haroon(as) with the Bani-Israel as his representative. (Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-142) But when he came back he saw that in his absence the Bani-Israel had started worshipping the calf. (Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-148) Musa(as) was furious :\nفَرَجَعَ مُوسَىٰ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ غَضْبَانَ أَسِفًا\nSo Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved.\n(Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-86)\nقَالَ يَا هَارُونُ مَا مَنَعَكَ إِذْ رَأَيْتَهُمْ ضَلُّوا\n[Moses] said, \"O Aaron, what prevented you, when you saw them going astray?\n(Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-92)\nMusa(as) took hold of the beard of his brother in anger. Then Haroon(as) said:\nقَالَ يَا ابْنَ أُمَّ لَا تَأْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِي وَلَا بِرَأْسِي ۖ إِنِّي خَشِيتُ أَن تَقُولَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِي\n[Aaron] said, \"O son of my mother, do not seize [me] by my beard or by my head. Indeed, I feared that you would say, 'You caused division among the Children of Israel, and you did not observe [or await] my word.' \"\n(Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-94)\nAt another place it says:\nوَلَمَّا رَجَعَ مُوسَىٰ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ غَضْبَانَ أَسِفًا قَالَ بِئْسَمَا خَلَفْتُمُونِي مِن بَعْدِي ۖ أَعَجِلْتُمْ أَمْرَ رَبِّكُمْ ۖ وَأَلْقَى الْأَلْوَاحَ وَأَخَذَ بِرَأْسِ أَخِيهِ يَجُرُّهُ إِلَيْهِ ۚ قَالَ ابْنَ أُمَّ إِنَّ الْقَوْمَ اسْتَضْعَفُونِي وَكَادُوا يَقْتُلُونَنِي فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِيَ الْأَعْدَاءَ وَلَا تَجْعَلْنِي مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ\nAnd when Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved, he said, \"How wretched is that by which you have replaced me after [my departure]. Were you impatient over the matter of your Lord?\" And he threw down the tablets and seized his brother by [the hair of] his head, pulling him toward him. [Aaron] said, \"O son of my mother, indeed the people oppressed me and were about to kill me, so let not the enemies rejoice over me and do not place me among the wrongdoing people.\"\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-150)\nIt is clear from the Holy Quran that Haroon(as) was not involved in either the making or the worshipping of the calf. But he did not firmly stop the Bani-Israel fearing a division among them. So, Musa(as) behaved roughly with him. Along with other distortions in the Taurah, this incident is also wrongly described by attributing the making and worshipping of the calf to Haroon(as). (See Exodus: 32)\nMentioning wrong facts about the prophets has been severely criticized in the Holy Quran while also presenting the correct version:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ ١١٤ وَنَجَّيْنَاهُمَا وَقَوْمَهُمَا مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيمِ ١١٥ وَنَصَرْنَاهُمْ فَكَانُوا هُمُ الْغَالِبِينَ ١١٦ وَآتَيْنَاهُمَا الْكِتَابَ الْمُسْتَبِينَ ١١٧ وَهَدَيْنَاهُمَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ ١١٨ وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِمَا فِي الْآخِرِينَ ١١٩ سَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ ١٢٠ إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ ١٢١ إِنَّهُمَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ١٢٢﴾\nAnd We did certainly confer favor upon Moses and Aaron. And We saved them and their people from the great affliction, And We supported them so it was they who overcame. And We gave them the explicit Scripture, And We guided them on the straight path. And We left for them [favorable mention] among later generations: \"Peace upon Moses and Aaron.\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good. Indeed, they were of Our believing servants.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-114-122)\nWe come to know from the Taurah that the Bani-Israel selected Haroon(as) as their first priest.( See Exodus, 40:12-15) and he held this post for forty years. After him his son took over. He died at the age of 123. His grave is on some peak of Sina. A mosque has been built there and the mountain is called ‘Haroon mountain’. We also come to know from Taurah that he died before Musa(as). (See Numbers, 20:22-29)\nThe other Haroon who is described in the Holy Quran is the brother of Maryam who scolds her and says:\nيَا أُخْتَ هَارُونَ مَا كَانَ أَبُوكِ امْرَأَ سَوْءٍ وَمَا كَانَتْ أُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا\n“O sister of Aaron, your father was not a man of evil, nor was your mother unchaste.\"\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verse-28)"],[128,"§Haroon’s sister\nIn the Holy Quran, the mother of Isa(as), Maryam has been called Haroon’s sister. According to the religious books, neither man nor jinn touched Maryam, but she became an unmarried mother. This is a great miracle of Allah(swt). When she went with the baby boy to the people of her tribe, they chastised her and called her the sister of Haroon. The Holy Quran describes this as follows:\n﴿فَأَتَتْ بِهِ قَوْمَهَا تَحْمِلُهُ ۖ قَالُوا يَا مَرْيَمُ لَقَدْ جِئْتِ شَيْئًا فَرِيًّا ٢٧ يَا أُخْتَ هَارُونَ مَا كَانَ أَبُوكِ امْرَأَ سَوْءٍ وَمَا كَانَتْ أُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا ٢٨﴾\nThen she brought him to her people, carrying him. They said, \"O Mary, you have certainly done a thing unprecedented. O sister of Aaron, your father was not a man of evil, nor was your mother unchaste.\"\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-27-28)\nWho was this Haroon? There is a difference of opinion among the scholars regarding this. Some feel that the person meant here is the brother of Musa(as) because Maryam was from the same tribe and by calling her the sister of Haroon, the people are trying to make her feel ashamed that even though she belonged to the tribe of Haroon the prophet, she had committed a shameful act.\nThe second opinion is that Maryam had a brother named Haroon who was known for his excellent character. Some people may have known him because we have very little knowledge about Maryam and her family tree. This is corroborated in one hadith which Muslim has also narrated in his sahih hadith that people named their children after prophets and pious people. So, it is possible that Maryam had a brother named Haroon.(Sahih Muslim, The Book on General Behaviour-9, 3:1785)\nThe third opinion is that Haroon was some blameless character in Bani-Israel. Maryam was not his actual sister but was from the same tribe. This is the opinion of Qatada and some other scholars. This type of language is used in other places also in the Holy Quran. For example:\nوَإِلَىٰ عَادٍ أَخَاهُمْ هُودًا\nAnd to the 'Aad [We sent] their brother Hud.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-65)\nHud(as) was not the brother of the entire tribe; but he has been called their brother just as in the case of Haroon and Maryam."],[129,"§Hawaari\nThe word ‘Hawaari’ is derived from ‘Hoar’ which means ‘white’. ‘Hur’ is derived from this which means ‘fair-skinned’ women. These ‘Hawaari’ were the companions of Isa(as). It is possible that they wore white clothes and were therefore called ‘Hawaari’. That is why the priest wears white clothes. It may also mean ‘helpers’ or ‘disciples’, as we understand from the following hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Every prophet has disciples(hawaaris) and my(saws) disciple(hawaari) is Az-Zubair bin Al-Awwam.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 2846 and Muslim, 2115)\nJust as the Ansar were the helpers of the Holy Prophet(saws) and the Muslims, the ‘Hawaaris’ were the helpers of Isa(as):\nReferring to this the Holy Quran says:\nفَلَمَّا أَحَسَّ عِيسَىٰ مِنْهُمُ الْكُفْرَ قَالَ مَنْ أَنصَارِي إِلَى اللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنصَارُ اللَّهِ آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَاشْهَدْ بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ\nBut when Jesus felt [persistence in] disbelief from them, he said, \"Who are my supporters for [the cause of] Allah?\" The disciples said, \"We are supporters for Allah. We have believed in Allah and testify that we are Muslims [submitting to Him].\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-52)\nAddressing the believers, Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُونُوا أَنصَارَ اللَّهِ كَمَا قَالَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ لِلْحَوَارِيِّينَ مَنْ أَنصَارِي إِلَى اللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنصَارُ اللَّهِ\nO you who have believed, be supporters of Allah, as when Jesus, the son of Mary, said to the disciples, \"Who are my supporters for Allah?\" The disciples said, \"We are supporters of Allah.\"\n(Quran, Surah-61, As-Saff, Verse-14)\nIt was the mercy and kindness of Allah(swt) that He put it in the heart of the ‘Hawaaris’ to believe in Him(swt) and His(swt) prophet Isa(as) because the Bani-Israel had called Isa(as) a magician and rejected his prophethood:\nوَإِذْ أَوْحَيْتُ إِلَى الْحَوَارِيِّينَ أَنْ آمِنُوا بِي وَبِرَسُولِي قَالُوا آمَنَّا وَاشْهَدْ بِأَنَّنَا مُسْلِمُونَ\nAnd [remember] when I inspired to the disciples, \"Believe in Me and in My messenger Jesus.\" They said, \"We have believed, so bear witness that indeed we are Muslims [in submission to Allah].\"\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-111)\nAnd Allah(swt) describes a conversation between Isa(as) and the ‘Hawaaris’ in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِذْ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ يَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ هَلْ يَسْتَطِيعُ رَبُّكَ أَن يُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنَا مَائِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ ۖ قَالَ اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ١١٢ قَالُوا نُرِيدُ أَن نَّأْكُلَ مِنْهَا وَتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُنَا وَنَعْلَمَ أَن قَدْ صَدَقْتَنَا وَنَكُونَ عَلَيْهَا مِنَ الشَّاهِدِينَ ١١٣ قَالَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ اللَّهُمَّ رَبَّنَا أَنزِلْ عَلَيْنَا مَائِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ تَكُونُ لَنَا عِيدًا لِّأَوَّلِنَا وَآخِرِنَا وَآيَةً مِّنكَ ۖ وَارْزُقْنَا وَأَنتَ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِينَ ١١٤ قَالَ اللَّهُ إِنِّي مُنَزِّلُهَا عَلَيْكُمْ ۖ فَمَن يَكْفُرْ بَعْدُ مِنكُمْ فَإِنِّي أُعَذِّبُهُ عَذَابًا لَّا أُعَذِّبُهُ أَحَدًا مِّنَ الْعَالَمِينَ ١١٥﴾\n[And remember] when the disciples said, \"O Jesus, Son of Mary, can your Lord send down to us a table [spread with food] from the heaven? [Jesus] said, \"Fear Allah, if you should be believers.\" They said, \"We wish to eat from it and let our hearts be reassured and know that you have been truthful to us and be among its witnesses.\" Said Jesus, the son of Mary, \"O Allah, our Lord, send down to us a table [spread with food] from the heaven to be for us a festival for the first of us and the last of us and a sign from You. And provide for us, and You are the best of providers.\" Allah said, \"Indeed, I will sent it down to you, but whoever disbelieves afterwards from among you - then indeed will I punish him with a punishment by which I have not punished anyone among the worlds.\"\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-112-115)\nFrom the above conversation it appears that the faith of the ‘Hawaaris’ was a little unsteady and they wanted to witness a miracle from Allah(swt) in order to strengthen their faith and that is why they made a request for a spread from heaven."],[130,"§Help(Wasila or means of approach)\nHelp or Wasila means seeking someone’s help in order to gain favor with Allah(swt). Before Islam and even today, when people are stopped from worshipping others besides Allah(swt), they say that they are worshipping others to please them merely to take their help in getting closer to Allah(swt).\nReferring to this, the Holy Quran says:\nأَلَا لِلَّهِ الدِّينُ الْخَالِصُ ۚ وَالَّذِينَ اتَّخَذُوا مِن دُونِهِ أَوْلِيَاءَ مَا نَعْبُدُهُمْ إِلَّا لِيُقَرِّبُونَا إِلَى اللَّهِ زُلْفَىٰ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ فِي مَا هُمْ فِيهِ يَخْتَلِفُونَ\nUnquestionably, for Allah is the pure religion. And those who take protectors besides Him [say], \"We only worship them that they may bring us nearer to Allah in position.\" Indeed, Allah will judge between them concerning that over which they differ.\n(Quran, Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-3)\nThe Holy Quran condemns all these blind beliefs and explains clearly that all worship is for Allah(swt) alone and that does not mean going to some saint or other deities or to some grave. If someone wants to get closer to Allah(swt) that is, gain His(swt) pleasure, it can be done in three ways:\nOne means of approach to get closer to Allah(swt) is with the help of good and pious deeds as mentioned in the Holy Quran:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَابْتَغُوا إِلَيْهِ الْوَسِيلَةَ وَجَاهِدُوا فِي سَبِيلِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ\nO you who have believed, fear Allah and seek the means [of nearness] to Him and strive in His cause that you may succeed.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-35)\nIn the above verse, it has been commanded to fear Allah(swt) and fight in His(swt) cause(jihad) which are very pious deeds. In the same way we can gain the pleasure of Allah(swt) with the help of other good deeds. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿قُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِينَ زَعَمْتُم مِّن دُونِهِ فَلَا يَمْلِكُونَ كَشْفَ الضُّرِّ عَنكُمْ وَلَا تَحْوِيلًا ٥٦ أُولَٰئِكَ الَّذِينَ يَدْعُونَ يَبْتَغُونَ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمُ الْوَسِيلَةَ أَيُّهُمْ أَقْرَبُ وَيَرْجُونَ رَحْمَتَهُ وَيَخَافُونَ عَذَابَهُ ۚ إِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ كَانَ مَحْذُورًا ٥٧﴾\nSay, \"Invoke those you have claimed [as gods] besides Him, for they do not possess the [ability for] removal of adversity from you or [for its] transfer [to someone else].\" Those whom they invoke seek means of access to their Lord, [striving as to] which of them would be nearest, and they hope for His mercy and fear His punishment. Indeed, the punishment of your Lord is ever feared.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verses-56-57)\nThere is a hadith about the above verse narrated by Abdullah-bin-Masood that the reason why it was revealed was that some people worshipped the jinn. But these jinn have become Muslims and they themselves were seeking ways to get nearer to Allah(swt) and the people who were worshipping them were not aware of this.(Sahih Bukhari 4714 and Muslim 3030)\nTaking the help of one’s good deeds is illustrated with the help of a popular hadith called ‘Hadith-e-Gar’. According to it, three people are trapped in a cave and the mouth of the cave gets covered with a huge boulder. Then, one by one all three of them think about some good deed of theirs which they had done just for pleasing Allah(swt) and then they pray to Allah(swt) that they had done the good deed just for pleasing Him(swt) and to please help them out of the cave. The boulder moves away from the mouth of the cave and the three of them manage to come out. (See Bukhari 2215 and Muslim 2742)\nThe second means of approach is using the most beautiful names of Allah(swt) as explained in the Holy Quran:\nوَلِلَّهِ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ فَادْعُوهُ بِهَا ۖ وَذَرُوا الَّذِينَ يُلْحِدُونَ فِي أَسْمَائِهِ ۚ سَيُجْزَوْنَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ\nAnd to Allah belong the best names, so invoke Him by them. And leave [the company of] those who practice deviation concerning His names. They will be recompensed for what they have been doing.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-180)\nIn the Sahih Hadith, it has been advised to pray and supplicate to Allah(swt) using His(swt) most beautiful names which is a way to have our prayers answered.\nThe third way is to ask some pious person to pray for us so that with the help of that person’s prayers our wishes are granted.\nDuring his(saws) lifetime, people would come to the Holy Prophet(saws) asking him to pray for them. After his(saws) death, Umar bin Al-Khattab(ra) prayed taking the help of the uncle of the Holy Prophet(saws), Abbas as:\n\"O Allah! We used to ask our Prophet to invoke You for rain, and You would bless us with rain, and now we ask his uncle to invoke you for rain. O Allah! Bless us with rain.\" And so it would rain.\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 1010)\nOther than these three approaches, there is no other way to get closer to Allah(swt). For example taking the help of the high position of some prophet or pious person or going to some grave. And we should not even take the help of some dead person because neither the Holy Prophet(saws) nor his(saws) companions ever did it. Wasila is connected with faith and any matter in this respect has to be accepted only after researching it thoroughly and it is a known fact that the people who do ‘bidaat’ do not have any basis for it.\n‘Wasila’ is also used for a she-camel who delivers both a male and a female camel at the same time. A she-camel who delivers she-camels twice and is left free in the name of some god or goddess is also called a ‘wasila’.\nReferring to this, the Holy Quran says:\nمَا جَعَلَ اللَّهُ مِن بَحِيرَةٍ وَلَا سَائِبَةٍ وَلَا وَصِيلَةٍ وَلَا حَامٍ ۙ وَلَٰكِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يَفْتَرُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ ۖ وَأَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُونَ\nAllah has not appointed [such innovations as] bahirah or sa'ibah or wasilah or ham. But those who disbelieve invent falsehood about Allah, and most of them do not reason.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-103)"],[131,"§Hijrat\n‘Hijrat’ means to emigrate from one land and seek refuge in another for the sake of Allah(swt). Ibraheem(as) said:\nوَقَالَ إِنِّي مُهَاجِرٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّي ۖ إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ\n[Abraham] said, \"Indeed, I will emigrate to [the service of] my Lord. Indeed, He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\"\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-26)\nIt became difficult for Ibraheem(as) to live among the idol-worshippers and pray to the One and Only God Allah(swt), therefore he left his homeland and migrated to Palestine.\nIn the history of Islam the first ‘Hijrat’ was from Makka to Ethiopia by a group of 11 men and 4 women. This was in the fifth year of the Holy Prophet(saws)’s prophethood. When it became difficult for the Muslims to stay on in Makka, the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“The King of Ethiopia does not torment the people. So, you go and stay there till the difficult times are over.” (See: Ibn-Hisham, 1:334)\nAfter some time the people in Ethiopia got the news that the people of Makka had accepted Islam. So, some of them returned. Usman-bin-Maz’oon was among them. But this was just a rumour. So, these people went back to Ethiopia and this time there were 80 people with them. This is called the second hijrat. But the disbelievers of Makka could not digest the fact that the Muslims were living peacefully in Ethiopia. So, they sent messengers to the king asking him to send back the refugees from Makka. When the king asked the immigrants about their new religion, Zafar-bin-Abu Talib gave a soul-stirring description as follows:\n“O King! We were idol-worshippers worshipping multiple gods and goddesses. We were eating dead animals; we were committing excesses against our neighbors; we were thirsty for each others’ blood; we did not know the difference between lawful and unlawful things; and then Allah(swt) sent a person from our tribe – a person well-known for truthfulness and trustworthiness- as a prophet. This person preached the worship of the One True God; forbade ‘shirk’ and advocated love towards neighbors and relatives.”\nThe Ethiopian king said, “Recite something of what has been revealed to him.”\nThen, Zafar(ra) recited a few verses of the 19th surah, Maryam. Upon hearing them, tears started flowing out of the king’s eyes and his beard became wet. The priest sitting in his court also broke down. The king said, ”This is the same thing which was revealed to Isa(as) because in fact both are the rays from the same source of light. O refugees go forth in my land and live as you please.”\nThe most famous hijrat is the one undertaken by the Holy Prophet(saws) from Makka to Madina when it became impossible for him to stay on in Makka. This hijrat has been described as the most important year in Islamic history by the caliph Umar(ra).\nAt that time, the people who did not migrate were criticized. As for the people who could not migrate due to some constraint, it was a different matter. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَفَّاهُمُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ ظَالِمِي أَنفُسِهِمْ قَالُوا فِيمَ كُنتُمْ ۖ قَالُوا كُنَّا مُسْتَضْعَفِينَ فِي الْأَرْضِ ۚ قَالُوا أَلَمْ تَكُنْ أَرْضُ اللَّهِ وَاسِعَةً فَتُهَاجِرُوا فِيهَا ۚ فَأُولَٰئِكَ مَأْوَاهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ ۖ وَسَاءَتْ مَصِيرًا ٩٧ إِلَّا الْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَاءِ وَالْوِلْدَانِ لَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ حِيلَةً وَلَا يَهْتَدُونَ سَبِيلًا ٩٨ فَأُولَٰئِكَ عَسَى اللَّهُ أَن يَعْفُوَ عَنْهُمْ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَفُوًّا غَفُورًا ٩٩﴾\nIndeed, those whom the angels take [in death] while wronging themselves - [the angels] will say, \"In what [condition] were you?\" They will say, \"We were oppressed in the land.\" The angels will say, \"Was not the earth of Allah spacious [enough] for you to emigrate therein?\" For those, their refuge is Hell - and evil it is as a destination. Except for the oppressed among men, women and children who cannot devise a plan nor are they directed to a way - For those it is expected that Allah will pardon them, and Allah is ever Pardoning and Forgiving.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verses-97-99)\nIn the succeeding verse, the immigrants are being given consolation and courage that they shall not face any hardship in the new land and that they would find ample means of sustenance:\nوَمَن يُهَاجِرْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ يَجِدْ فِي الْأَرْضِ مُرَاغَمًا كَثِيرًا وَسَعَةً ۚ وَمَن يَخْرُجْ مِن بَيْتِهِ مُهَاجِرًا إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ ثُمَّ يُدْرِكْهُ الْمَوْتُ فَقَدْ وَقَعَ أَجْرُهُ عَلَى اللَّهِ ۗ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ غَفُورًا رَّحِيمًا\nAnd whoever emigrates for the cause of Allah will find on the earth many [alternative] locations and abundance. And whoever leaves his home as an emigrant to Allah and His Messenger and then death overtakes him - his reward has already become incumbent upon Allah. And Allah is ever Forgiving and Merciful.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-100)\nAfter the triumph over Makka in 8 A.H and the subsequent reversion of all the people of Makka to Islam, there was no need for immigration. So, the Holy Prophet(saws) made the following announcement:\n“After the victory there will be no more hijrat but there will be jihad. So, if you are called for jihad, go forth.” (Sahih Bukhari: 1834, Muslim: 1353)\nThat is, it was the end of hijrat from Makka to Madina. But even today if in any part of the world, Muslims are being tormented and are not able to freely practice their religion, then it is a must for them to migrate to some place where the conditions are better."],[132,"§Hijri\nThis was the year when the Holy Prophet(saws) migrated from Makka to Madina following the command of Allah(swt). The second caliph Hazrat Umar(ra) described this as the most important event in Islamic history due to which the Muslims had to face great hardships. He started the hijri Islamic calendar dated from the year of this migration. (See ‘Hijrat’)"],[133,"§Honey\nHoney is a viscous liquid secreted by the honey-bees after sucking the nectar of the flowers. Allah(swt) has blessed honey with many curative properties. Many research papers about the benefits of honey have been published. It is astonishing that about fifteen hundred years back, the things which are being discovered today had been mentioned so clearly in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَأَوْحَىٰ رَبُّكَ إِلَى النَّحْلِ أَنِ اتَّخِذِي مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًا وَمِنَ الشَّجَرِ وَمِمَّا يَعْرِشُونَ ٦٨ ثُمَّ كُلِي مِن كُلِّ الثَّمَرَاتِ فَاسْلُكِي سُبُلَ رَبِّكِ ذُلُلًا ۚ يَخْرُجُ مِن بُطُونِهَا شَرَابٌ مُّخْتَلِفٌ أَلْوَانُهُ فِيهِ شِفَاءٌ لِّلنَّاسِ ۗ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَآيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٦٩﴾\nAnd your Lord inspired to the bee, \"Take for yourself among the mountains, houses, and among the trees and [in] that which they construct. Then eat from all the fruits and follow the ways of your Lord laid down [for you].\" There emerges from their bellies a drink, varying in colors, in which there is healing for people. Indeed in that is a sign for a people who give thought.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verses-68,69)\nThis is one of the miracles of the Holy Quran. It is due to this uniqueness of honey that a surah is named surah An-Nahl. Honey has been described only once in this surah. Most of the surah is about monotheism and its various proofs and the life-cycle of the honey-bee is in itself a sign of monotheism."],[134,"§Hoor\nAmong the attractions of paradise which have been created for the pious Muslims, ‘Hoor’ or ‘fair-skinned damsels’ are one.\nThe meaning of ‘hoor’ is beautiful women, the black of whose eyes is very black and the whites of their eyes is very white.\nIn the Arabic language. ‘hoor’ means ‘beautiful and pretty women.’ The Holy Quran describes their qualities as follows:\n1. They will have large doe-shaped eyes. That is why they have been called ‘hoor-e-ayn’ (large eyed women). (Quran, Surah-44, Ad-Dukhan, Verse-54 and Surah-52, At-Tur, Verse-20)\n2. They will be women with lowered eyes; that is very modest. The Holy Quran says:\nفِيهِنَّ قَاصِرَاتُ الطَّرْفِ لَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ إِنسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَانٌّ\n“They will be women with lowered eyes whom no man or jinn had ever touched.”\n3. Their beauty will be like rubies and coral. The Holy Quran says:\nكَأَنَّهُنَّ الْيَاقُوتُ وَالْمَرْجَانُ\nAs if they were rubies and coral.\n4. They will be good and beautiful. The Holy Quran says:\nفِيهِنَّ خَيْرَاتٌ حِسَانٌ\nIn them are good and beautiful women.\n5. They will be staying in tents. The Holy Quran says:\nحُورٌ مَّقْصُورَاتٌ فِي الْخِيَامِ\nFair ones reserved in pavilions.\n6. Untouched before them by man or jinni. The Holy Quran says:\nلَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ إِنسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَانٌّ\nThat is they will be virgins. In fact, nobody would have even touched them.\n(See: Quran, Surah-55, Ar-Rahman, Verses-56,58,70,72,74)"],[135,"§Horse\nIn the Holy Quran, two words have been used for the horse:\nOne is ‘Jiyad’. The story of Sulaiman(as) has been described in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِذْ عُرِضَ عَلَيْهِ بِالْعَشِيِّ الصَّافِنَاتُ الْجِيَادُ ٣١ فَقَالَ إِنِّي أَحْبَبْتُ حُبَّ الْخَيْرِ عَن ذِكْرِ رَبِّي حَتَّىٰ تَوَارَتْ بِالْحِجَابِ ٣٢﴾\n[Mention] when there were exhibited before him in the afternoon the poised [standing] racehorses. And he said, \"Indeed, I gave preference to the love of good [things] over the remembrance of my Lord until the sun disappeared into the curtain [of darkness].\"\n(Quran, Surah-38, Saad, Verse-31,32)\nFor a more detailed explanation see ‘Sulaiman’.\nThe other word is ‘Khail’ which also means a horse. This word has been used at various places in various contexts. At one place it says:\nزُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ الشَّهَوَاتِ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ وَالْبَنِينَ وَالْقَنَاطِيرِ الْمُقَنطَرَةِ مِنَ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ وَالْخَيْلِ الْمُسَوَّمَةِ وَالْأَنْعَامِ وَالْحَرْثِ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ مَتَاعُ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا ۖ وَاللَّهُ عِندَهُ حُسْنُ الْمَآبِ\nBeautified for people is the love of that which they desire - of women and sons, heaped-up sums of gold and silver, fine branded horses, and cattle and tilled land. That is the enjoyment of worldly life, but Allah has with Him the best return.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-14)\nAt another place it says:\nوَأَعِدُّوا لَهُم مَّا اسْتَطَعْتُم مِّن قُوَّةٍ وَمِن رِّبَاطِ الْخَيْلِ تُرْهِبُونَ بِهِ عَدُوَّ اللَّهِ وَعَدُوَّكُمْ وَآخَرِينَ مِن دُونِهِمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَهُمُ اللَّهُ يَعْلَمُهُمْ\nAnd prepare against them whatever you are able of power and of steeds of war by which you may terrify the enemy of Allah and your enemy and others besides them whom you do not know [but] whom Allah knows.\n(Quran, Surah-8, Al-Anfal, Verse-60)\nThis is because in those times wars were fought by soldiers mounted on horses.\nThe Holy Quran says:\nوَالْخَيْلَ وَالْبِغَالَ وَالْحَمِيرَ لِتَرْكَبُوهَا وَزِينَةً\nAnd [He created] the horses, mules and donkeys for you to ride and [as] adornment.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-8)\nPraising the horses, the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَالْعَادِيَاتِ ضَبْحًا ١ فَالْمُورِيَاتِ قَدْحًا ٢ فَالْمُغِيرَاتِ صُبْحًا ٣ فَأَثَرْنَ بِهِ نَقْعًا ٤ فَوَسَطْنَ بِهِ جَمْعًا ٥ إِنَّ الْإِنسَانَ لِرَبِّهِ لَكَنُودٌ ٦﴾\nBy the racers, panting, And the producers of sparks [when] striking .And the chargers at dawn, Stirring up thereby [clouds of] dust, Arriving thereby in the center collectively, Indeed mankind, to his Lord, is ungrateful.\n(Quran, Surah-100, Al-Adiyat, Verses-1-6)\nIn these verses, swearing by the horse, the ungratefulness of man is being highlighted. Not caring for its life, a horse just charges ahead in a war when its master orders it to do so. But man is so ungrateful that even though Allah(swt) has created this whole world and bestowed innumerable favors upon him, he does not remember Him(swt). Allah(swt) warns the people who have become heedless of Him(swt) in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّ الْإِنسَانَ لِرَبِّهِ لَكَنُودٌ ٦ وَإِنَّهُ عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكَ لَشَهِيدٌ ٧ وَإِنَّهُ لِحُبِّ الْخَيْرِ لَشَدِيدٌ ٨ ۞ أَفَلَا يَعْلَمُ إِذَا بُعْثِرَ مَا فِي الْقُبُورِ ٩ وَحُصِّلَ مَا فِي الصُّدُورِ ١٠ إِنَّ رَبَّهُم بِهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ لَّخَبِيرٌ ١١﴾\nIndeed mankind, to his Lord, is ungrateful. And indeed, he is to that a witness. And indeed he is, in love of wealth, intense. But does he not know that when the contents of the graves are scattered And that within the breasts is obtained, Indeed, their Lord with them, that Day, is [fully] Acquainted.\n(Quran, Surah-100, Al-Adiyat, Verses-6-11)"],[136,"§Hospitality\nHospitality is given a lot of importance in Islam. The honoured guests of Ibraheem(as) are described as follows in the Holy Quran:\n﴿هَلْ أَتَاكَ حَدِيثُ ضَيْفِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ الْمُكْرَمِينَ ٢٤ إِذْ دَخَلُوا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوا سَلَامًا ۖ قَالَ سَلَامٌ قَوْمٌ مُّنكَرُونَ ٢٥ فَرَاغَ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهِ فَجَاءَ بِعِجْلٍ سَمِينٍ ٢٦ فَقَرَّبَهُ إِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ أَلَا تَأْكُلُونَ ٢٧﴾\nHas there reached you the story of the honored guests of Abraham? When they entered upon him and said, \"[We greet you with] peace.\" He answered, \"[And upon you] peace, [you are] a people unknown. Then he went to his family and came with a fat [roasted] calf .And placed it near them; he said, \"Will you not eat?\"\n(Quran, Surah-51, Adh-Dhariyat, Verses-24-27)\nThese guests were in fact angels who had come to Ibraheem(as) to give him the glad tidings of a son who would be born to his wife. The way Ibraheem(as) welcomed his guests with a roasted calf shows the importance which was given to guests in those days.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) has also explained the importance of guests in various ways. According to one Sahih Hadith:\n“Whoever believes in Allah(swt) and the Last Day should show hospitality to his guests.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5185 and Sahih Muslim, 74)\nBut the guests also have certain responsibilities. One of them is that the guest should not stay for more than three days. The hadith says that for one day and one night the guest should be treated with the greatest honor. After that for the next two days, he should be fed with whatever is available. If the guest needs to stay for more than three days, just as the host is being charitable to him, the guest should also not consider himself a guest. (Abu Dawood, 3738)\nAccording to another hadith:\n“Hospitality is for three days, after that it is sadaqah or charity.”\n(Abu Dawood: 3749)"],[137,"§House-fly\nHouse-fly belongs to one of the lowest species of animals. It is mostly found in the eastern countries where the climate is hot. While it is generally irritating and is a carrier of many diseases, some species are also poisonous.\nIt is described twice in the same verse of the Holy Quran and in both cases it is used as an example for insignificance:\nيَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ ضُرِبَ مَثَلٌ فَاسْتَمِعُوا لَهُ ۚ إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ لَن يَخْلُقُوا ذُبَابًا وَلَوِ اجْتَمَعُوا لَهُ ۖ وَإِن يَسْلُبْهُمُ الذُّبَابُ شَيْئًا لَّا يَسْتَنقِذُوهُ مِنْهُ ۚ ضَعُفَ الطَّالِبُ وَالْمَطْلُوبُ\nO people, an example is presented, so listen to it. Indeed, those you invoke besides Allah will never create [as much as] a fly, even if they gathered together for that purpose. And if the fly should steal away from them a [tiny] thing, they could not recover it from him. Weak are the pursuer and pursued.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-73)\nThis example is a lesson for people who have made deities of false gods and goddesses, graves, stones etc. and invoke them and imagine them to be their saviours."],[138,"§Hud(as)\nHud(as) was one of the prophets of Arabia. He was the first prophet to be sent to the people of Arabia after Nuh(as). His tribe was ‘Aad’ which was one of the biggest tribes after Nuh(as):\n﴿وَإِلَىٰ عَادٍ أَخَاهُمْ هُودًا ۗ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۚ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ٦٥ قَالَ الْمَلَأُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِن قَوْمِهِ إِنَّا لَنَرَاكَ فِي سَفَاهَةٍ وَإِنَّا لَنَظُنُّكَ مِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ ٦٦ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ لَيْسَ بِي سَفَاهَةٌ وَلَٰكِنِّي رَسُولٌ مِّن رَّبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٦٧ أُبَلِّغُكُمْ رِسَالَاتِ رَبِّي وَأَنَا لَكُمْ نَاصِحٌ أَمِينٌ ٦٨ أَوَعَجِبْتُمْ أَن جَاءَكُمْ ذِكْرٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٍ مِّنكُمْ لِيُنذِرَكُمْ ۚ وَاذْكُرُوا إِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَاءَ مِن بَعْدِ قَوْمِ نُوحٍ وَزَادَكُمْ فِي الْخَلْقِ بَسْطَةً ۖ فَاذْكُرُوا آلَاءَ اللَّهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٦٩﴾\nAnd to the 'Aad [We sent] their brother Hud. He said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. Then will you not fear Him?\" Said the eminent ones who disbelieved among his people, \"Indeed, we see you in foolishness, and indeed, we think you are of the liars.\" [Hud] said, \"O my people, there is not foolishness in me, but I am a messenger from the Lord of the worlds.\" I convey to you the messages of my Lord, and I am to you a trustworthy adviser. Then do you wonder that there has come to you a reminder from your Lord through a man from among you, that he may warn you? And remember when He made you successors after the people of Noah and increased you in stature extensively. So remember the favors of Allah that you might succeed.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verses-65-69)\nFrom the above verses we understand that the tribe of Aad towards which Hud(as) was sent as a messenger was a tribe which lived after Nuh(as). Some historians hold the view that Hud(as) was the great grandson of Saam-bin-Nuh and the genealogy has been presented as follows:\nHud - son of Shalah - son of Arfakhshad - son of Sam – son of Nuh(as).\nNow is it possible that in just seven generations after the ‘Great Flood’, the tribe of Aad became so big and powerful unlike any other tribe? So, either the genealogy is not very reliable or the life-span of those people was more than ours because there are only three generations between the tribe of Aad and Hud(as). According to another historian, the genealogy is as follows:\nHud - son of Abdullah - son of Rubah - son of Haloos - son of Aad - son of A’oz - son of Aram - son of Sam – son of Nuh(as).\nWhatever the facts, it can be said that definitely the tribe of Aad was a very big tribe of those times. As to their territory, many feel that it was near Hadhramaut in Yemen which is now a barren desert. Some scholars are of the opinion that these people came out of Yemen and spread till Iraq and Syria. But this is not what we come to know from history because they were destroyed right in their homeland. And they were destroyed such that there was no trace left as is described later. And it does not seem correct to say that they were the builders of the great pyramids. But this was a very powerful tribe.\nفَأَمَّا عَادٌ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَقَالُوا مَنْ أَشَدُّ مِنَّا قُوَّةً ۖ أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا أَنَّ اللَّهَ الَّذِي خَلَقَهُمْ هُوَ أَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً ۖ وَكَانُوا بِآيَاتِنَا يَجْحَدُونَ\nAs for 'Aad, they were arrogant upon the earth without right and said, \"Who is greater than us in strength?\" Did they not consider that Allah who created them was greater than them in strength? But they were rejecting Our signs.\n(Quran, Surah-41, As-Sajda, Verse-15)\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِعَادٍ ٦ إِرَمَ ذَاتِ الْعِمَادِ ٧ الَّتِي لَمْ يُخْلَقْ مِثْلُهَا فِي الْبِلَادِ ٨﴾\nHave you not considered how your Lord dealt with 'Aad - [With] Iram - who had lofty pillars, The likes of whom had never been created in the land?\n(Quran, Surah-89, Al-Fajr, Verses-6-8)\nThat is, during the time of this tribe there was no other tribe like it. They would construct lofty pillars and were considered to be the most powerful people of those times. But when they started worshipping false gods and goddesses instead of the One true Allah(swt), and even after repeated warnings of prophet Hud(as) did not follow the true path and even called Hud(as) foolish and a liar, the punishment of Allah(swt) descended upon them and they were wiped out from the face of this earth as described later on. They had three main deities whom they worshipped: Samda, Samuda and Hara.\nAll the prophets preached monotheism. So, Hud(as) also forbade idol-worship and preached the worship of one Allah(swt), the Creator of the earth and the heavens, the Sustainer of everything. But like the other misled tribes, the tribe of Aad also rejected Hud(as) and refused to believe his words:\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ أَخَا عَادٍ إِذْ أَنذَرَ قَوْمَهُ بِالْأَحْقَافِ وَقَدْ خَلَتِ النُّذُرُ مِن بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوا إِلَّا اللَّهَ إِنِّي أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ٢١ قَالُوا أَجِئْتَنَا لِتَأْفِكَنَا عَنْ آلِهَتِنَا فَأْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَا إِن كُنتَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ ٢٢﴾\nAnd mention, [O Muhammad], the brother of 'Aad, when he warned his people in the [region of] al-Ahqaf - and warners had already passed on before him and after him - [saying], \"Do not worship except Allah. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a terrible day.\" They said, \"Have you come to delude us away from our gods? Then bring us what you promise us, if you should be of the truthful.\"\n(Quran, Surah-46, Al-Ahqaf, Verses-21,22)\nAhqaf is a desert located to the south of Arabia. This was fertile land once upon a time when the tribe of Aad lived there. Hud(as) had come there with the religion of God. But they rejected his message due to which they suffered the torment of Allah(swt). About this the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَفِي عَادٍ إِذْ أَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّيحَ الْعَقِيمَ ٤١ مَا تَذَرُ مِن شَيْءٍ أَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ إِلَّا جَعَلَتْهُ كَالرَّمِيمِ ٤٢﴾\nAnd in 'Aad [was a sign], when We sent against them the barren wind. It left nothing of what it came upon but that it made it like disintegrated ruins.\n(Quran, Surah-51, Adh-Dhariyat, Verses-41,42)\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿كَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِي وَنُذُرِ ١٨ إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيحًا صَرْصَرًا فِي يَوْمِ نَحْسٍ مُّسْتَمِرٍّ ١٩ تَنزِعُ النَّاسَ كَأَنَّهُمْ أَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ مُّنقَعِرٍ ٢٠ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِي وَنُذُرِ ٢١ وَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْآنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِن مُّدَّكِرٍ ٢٢﴾\n'Aad denied; and how [severe] were My punishment and warning. Indeed, We sent upon them a screaming wind on a day of continuous misfortune, Extracting the people as if they were trunks of palm trees uprooted. And how [severe] were My punishment and warning. And We have certainly made the Qur'an easy for remembrance, so is there any who will remember?\n(Quran, Surah-54, Al-Qamar, Verses-18-22)\n﴿وَأَمَّا عَادٌ فَأُهْلِكُوا بِرِيحٍ صَرْصَرٍ عَاتِيَةٍ ٦ سَخَّرَهَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَبْعَ لَيَالٍ وَثَمَانِيَةَ أَيَّامٍ حُسُومًا فَتَرَى الْقَوْمَ فِيهَا صَرْعَىٰ كَأَنَّهُمْ أَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ خَاوِيَةٍ ٧ فَهَلْ تَرَىٰ لَهُم مِّن بَاقِيَةٍ ٨﴾\nAnd as for 'Aad, they were destroyed by a screaming, violent wind. Which Allah imposed upon them for seven nights and eight days in succession, so you would see the people therein fallen as if they were hollow trunks of palm trees. Then do you see of them any remains?\n(Quran, Surah-69, Al-Haqqa, Verses-6-8)\nThis is the ultimate end of the tribes who have rejected the messengers sent by Allah(swt). Instead of worshipping Allah(swt) alone, they started invoking their false gods and goddesses and started perpetrating all sorts of sins. As to where Hud(as) and the believers went after the calamity, there is no information about it either in the Holy Quran or in the Sahih Hadith. That is why we cannot say for certain as to what happened. According to some people there are two graves in Hadhramaut, one is that of Hud(as) and the other is of Saleh(as). Some others are of the opinion that like the other prophets, Hud(as) went away to Makka and there he breathed his last. But this cannot be confirmed from any sahih hadith."],[139,"§Hud-Hud(hoopoe)\nHud-hud is a bird found mostly in Palestine. It has a long beak. It forages for food with the help of its beak. Worms and insects are its favorite food. That is why the tribe of Musa(as) considered it haram to eat it. In Islam it has been classified under unclean animals. In Islam it is forbidden to kill four kinds of animals – ants, honey-bees, hud-hud(hoopoes) and shrikes(sparrow-hawks).\n(See: Abu Dawood, 5267; Ibn-Maaja, 3224 and Ahmad, 3066)\nThe hud-hud has been described only once in the Holy Quran. In the story of Sulaiman(as), we come to know that he was given the power over jinn, men and birds. One day he was making a supervision of the birds when he saw that the hud-hud bird was absent. He then said:\n﴿وَتَفَقَّدَ الطَّيْرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِيَ لَا أَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ أَمْ كَانَ مِنَ الْغَائِبِينَ ٢٠ لَأُعَذِّبَنَّهُ عَذَابًا شَدِيدًا أَوْ لَأَذْبَحَنَّهُ أَوْ لَيَأْتِيَنِّي بِسُلْطَانٍ مُّبِينٍ ٢١﴾\nAnd he took attendance of the birds and said, \"Why do I not see the hoopoe - or is he among the absent? I will surely punish him with a severe punishment or slaughter him unless he brings me clear authorization.\"\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verses-20,21)\n(For the remaining story see ‘Sulaiman(as)’)"],[140,"§Hudood\n‘Hudood’ is the plural of ‘Hadd’ which means ‘limit’. That is, Allah(swt) has set some limits and it is forbidden to even approach them. These limits are His(swt) commands forbidding some things. The Holy Quran says:\nتِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ فَلَا تَقْرَبُوهَا\nThese are the limits [set by] Allah, so do not approach them.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-187)\nBut people cross these limits due to which there is unrest in this world. Various kinds of punishments have been prescribed for the transgressors so that peace is maintained in the human society. These limits are called ‘hudood’ and it is the duty of the Islamic ruler to ensure that these are not transgressed. Only then will the lives, property and dignity of the subjects be safeguarded. That is why maintaining the limits has been stressed in the sahih hadith:\n“Applying one of the prescribed penalties on earth is better than forty days of rain” (Ibn-Maaja 2537 and Musnad Ahmad 2:402)\nSo, we find that wherever the laws and limits of Allah(swt) are followed, there is peace and prosperity. Among the limits set are adultery, intoxicants, stealing, murder, threatening, dacoity etc. (For more information refer to the specific heading)."],[141,"§Ibadat\nIbadat means to serve, worship, pray, bow and humbly submit oneself to somebody.\nAmong the tenets of Islam, the main one is that it permits the worship of the One True God Allah(swt) only. This was preached by all the prophets. But this was distorted by the followers of these prophets. In fact the main instruction of all the prophets was that they should stop worshipping multiple gods and goddesses and worship the One True God Allah(swt). But the disbelievers of all the periods practiced polytheism in the false hope that they would intercede on their behalf on the day of resurrection. But in the Hereafter they will be disillusioned when the people whom they were worshipping will disown them. The worshippers of Jesus Christ have been described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ اللَّهُ يَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ أَأَنتَ قُلْتَ لِلنَّاسِ اتَّخِذُونِي وَأُمِّيَ إِلَٰهَيْنِ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ مَا يَكُونُ لِي أَنْ أَقُولَ مَا لَيْسَ لِي بِحَقٍّ ۚ إِن كُنتُ قُلْتُهُ فَقَدْ عَلِمْتَهُ ۚ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِي وَلَا أَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِكَ ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوبِ ١١٦ مَا قُلْتُ لَهُمْ إِلَّا مَا أَمَرْتَنِي بِهِ أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبَّكُمْ ۚ وَكُنتُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيدًا مَّا دُمْتُ فِيهِمْ ۖ فَلَمَّا تَوَفَّيْتَنِي كُنتَ أَنتَ الرَّقِيبَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ وَأَنتَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ ١١٧ إِن تُعَذِّبْهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ ۖ وَإِن تَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ فَإِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ ١١٨﴾\nAnd [beware the Day] when Allah will say, \"O Jesus, Son of Mary, did you say to the people, 'Take me and my mother as deities besides Allah?'\" He will say, \"Exalted are You! It was not for me to say that to which I have no right. If I had said it, You would have known it. You know what is within myself, and I do not know what is within Yourself. Indeed, it is You who is Knower of the unseen. I said not to them except what You commanded me - to worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord. And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them; but when You took me up, You were the Observer over them, and You are, over all things, Witness. If You should punish them - indeed they are Your servants; but if You forgive them - indeed it is You who is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-116-118)\nIn the same way the Holy Quran describes the argument which takes place between Ibraheem(as) who advocates monotheism and his polytheist father in which Ibraheem(as) asks his father to abandon his false deities and worship Allah(swt) alone.\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ صِدِّيقًا نَّبِيًّا ٤١ إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ يَا أَبَتِ لِمَ تَعْبُدُ مَا لَا يَسْمَعُ وَلَا يُبْصِرُ وَلَا يُغْنِي عَنكَ شَيْئًا ٤٢ يَا أَبَتِ إِنِّي قَدْ جَاءَنِي مِنَ الْعِلْمِ مَا لَمْ يَأْتِكَ فَاتَّبِعْنِي أَهْدِكَ صِرَاطًا سَوِيًّا ٤٣ يَا أَبَتِ لَا تَعْبُدِ الشَّيْطَانَ ۖ إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ كَانَ لِلرَّحْمَٰنِ عَصِيًّا ٤٤ يَا أَبَتِ إِنِّي أَخَافُ أَن يَمَسَّكَ عَذَابٌ مِّنَ الرَّحْمَٰنِ فَتَكُونَ لِلشَّيْطَانِ وَلِيًّا ٤٥ قَالَ أَرَاغِبٌ أَنتَ عَنْ آلِهَتِي يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ ۖ لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهِ لَأَرْجُمَنَّكَ ۖ وَاهْجُرْنِي مَلِيًّا ٤٦ قَالَ سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكَ ۖ سَأَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّي ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ بِي حَفِيًّا ٤٧ وَأَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ وَأَدْعُو رَبِّي عَسَىٰ أَلَّا أَكُونَ بِدُعَاءِ رَبِّي شَقِيًّا ٤٨ فَلَمَّا اعْتَزَلَهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ وَهَبْنَا لَهُ إِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ ۖ وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا نَبِيًّا ٤٩ وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُم مِّن رَّحْمَتِنَا وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ عَلِيًّا ٥٠﴾\nAnd mention in the Book [the story of] Abraham. Indeed, he was a man of truth and a prophet. [Mention] when he said to his father, \"O my father, why do you worship that which does not hear and does not see and will not benefit you at all? O my father, indeed there has come to me of knowledge that which has not come to you, so follow me; I will guide you to an even path. O my father, do not worship Satan. Indeed Satan has ever been, to the Most Merciful, disobedient. O my father, indeed I fear that there will touch you a punishment from the Most Merciful so you would be to Satan a companion [in Hellfire].\" [His father] said, \"Have you no desire for my gods, O Abraham? If you do not desist, I will surely stone you, so avoid me a prolonged time.\" [Abraham] said, \"Peace will be upon you. I will ask forgiveness for you of my Lord. Indeed, He is ever gracious to me. And I will leave you and those you invoke other than Allah and will invoke my Lord. I expect that I will not be in invocation to my Lord unhappy.\" So when he had left them and those they worshipped other than Allah, We gave him Isaac and Jacob, and each [of them] We made a prophet. And We gave them of Our mercy, and we made for them a reputation of high honor.\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-41-50)\nThis is the meaning of Ibadat as understood by most of the people and is one of the main principles of Islam and no other religion can even come close to the form of worship practiced by Muslims. But in a broader sense Ibadat means to live one’s life completely according to the rules laid down by Almighty Allah(swt). Whatever Allah(swt) has deemed halal(allowed) should be considered halal and whatever Allah(swt) has forbidden should be strictly avoided. We should not invoke anybody other than Allah(swt). This is corroborated by a Hasan hadith:\nAdi-bin-Haatim once came to the Holy Prophet(saws). He was wearing the crucifix on his neck so the Holy Prophet(saws) asked him to remove it.\nAdi narrates that he heard the Holy Prophet(saws) recite the verse 31 of the 9th surah ‘Taubah’ from the Holy Quran which says:\nThey take their priests and their anchorites to be their lords.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said “They do not worship them but if they ordain something as halal, they consider it halal and if they ordain something as haraam, they consider it haraam” that is, it is ibadat. (Hadith: Tirmizi, 3095).\nHuzaifa-bin-Yamaan and Ibn-Abbas and the other companions say that following the scholars and priests in matters of halal and haraam is in fact worshipping Allah(swt).\nThis proves that accepting the teachings of Islam whole-heartedly and adhering to them in both words and actions is Ibadat while denying Islam and following the path shown by others is nothing short of shirk or polytheism which is the greatest and an unforgivable sin."],[142,"§Iblees\nIblees is the nickname of the satan. It is derived from the Greek word ‘diabolos’ which means enemy, devil or slanderer. That is why in the Arabic translation of the Holy Bible, ‘Iblees’ is used for ‘diabolos’. In some places, the word ‘satan’ is used.(See: Khamoos Kitab Muqaddas, p.15). Some scholars are of the opinion that Iblees is derived from the Arabic word ‘Balas’ which means ‘to lose hope’.The word is used in this sense in many places in the Holy Quran.\n(See: Quran, Surah-30, Ar-Rum, Verse-12; Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-44).\nAccording to Ibn-Abbas, his actual name was ‘Azazeel’, but when he refused to prostrate before Adam(as), he incurred the wrath of Allah(swt) and was thereafter called ‘Iblees’. This has been described by Ibn-Jareer, Tabri etc.\nThe first description of Iblees in the Holy Quran is as follows:\nوَإِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ أَبَىٰ وَاسْتَكْبَرَ وَكَانَ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ\nAnd [mention] when We said to the angels, \"Prostrate before Adam\"; so they prostrated, except for Iblees. He refused and was arrogant and became of the disbelievers.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-34)\nThis verse has been wrongly translated by some people as ‘ he was of the disbelievers’ when actually it means ‘ he became a disbeliever’\nَكَانَ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ should be translated as ‘ مِنَالْكَافِرِينَصار ‘\nThere are many other verses in the Holy Quran in which the meaning is as in the above verse. For example (see Surah-29, Al-Ankabut, Verse-32)\nلَنُنَجِّيَنَّهُ وَأَهْلَهُ إِلَّا امْرَأَتَهُ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغَابِرِينَ\nWe will surely save him and his family, except his wife. She is to be of those who remain behind.\"\nSimilarly in Surah-56, Al-Waqi’a, Verse-6:\nفَكَانَتْ هَبَاءً مُّنبَثًّا\nAnd become dust dispersing.\nSimilarly in Surah-11, Hud, Verse-43:\nقَالَ سَآوِي إِلَىٰ جَبَلٍ يَعْصِمُنِي مِنَ الْمَاءِ ۚ قَالَ لَا عَاصِمَ الْيَوْمَ مِنْ أَمْرِ اللَّهِ إِلَّا مَن رَّحِمَ ۚ وَحَالَ بَيْنَهُمَا الْمَوْجُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُغْرَقِينَ\n[But] he said, \"I will take refuge on a mountain to protect me from the water.\" [Noah] said, \"There is no protector today from the decree of Allah, except for whom He gives mercy.\" And the waves came between them, and he was among the drowned. That is\nفَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُغْرَقِينَ actually means صارمِنَالْمُغْرَقِينَ. In all the above verses كَانَ should be taken to mean صار.\nWhy was Iblees so arrogant? This is described in the Holy Quran as follows :\nقَالَ أَنَا خَيْرٌ مِّنْهُ خَلَقْتَنِي مِن نَّارٍ وَخَلَقْتَهُ مِن طِينٍ\n[Satan] said, \"I am better than him. You created me from fire and created him from clay.\"\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-12)\nAnd in the Surah Hijr:\nقَالَ لَمْ أَكُن لِّأَسْجُدَ لِبَشَرٍ خَلَقْتَهُ مِن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ\nHe said, \"Never would I prostrate to a human whom You created out of clay from an altered black mud.\"\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-33)\nWe will elaborate the following:\nThe creatures who are addressed by the commandments of Allah(swt).\nThe tribe of Iblees.\nDoes the act of prostration of the angels before Adam(as) go against the concept of monotheism?\nWhen was the command to prostrate before Adam(as) given?\nWhat is the role of Iblees in this world?\nThe creatures who have been instructed by Allah(swt) are of three kinds:\nAngels\nJinn\nand\nHumans\nAngels are those creatures of Allah(swt) who have no power to do as they please. They cannot refuse to do whatever they have been asked to do. Day and night, they are engaged in the worship of Allah(swt) and in obeying His orders. The Holy Quran says in this regard:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ وَأَهْلِيكُمْ نَارًا وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ عَلَيْهَا مَلَائِكَةٌ غِلَاظٌ شِدَادٌ لَّا يَعْصُونَ اللَّهَ مَا أَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُونَ مَا يُؤْمَرُونَ\nO you who have believed, protect yourselves and your families from a Fire whose fuel is people and stones, over which are [appointed] angels, harsh and severe; they do not disobey Allah in what He commands them but do what they are commanded.\n(Quran, Surah-66, At-Tahrim, Verse-6)\nAs for the jinn and humans, they have been given the freedom to either obey or disobey Allah(swt). So these two kinds of creatures, namely the jinn and the humans are actually undergoing a test in this world. So, once they leave this world, the obedient ones will be rewarded with a happy life in paradise while the disobedient ones will be forever doomed to a painful life in hell.\nوَلَقَدْ ذَرَأْنَا لِجَهَنَّمَ كَثِيرًا مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنسِ\nAnd We have certainly created for Hell many of the jinn and mankind.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-179)\nThat is, hell has been created for the ones who have defied the Sovereignty of Allah(swt) or ascribed partners to Him while the heaven has been created for the ones who have truly submitted to the will of Allah(swt) alone.\nThe ones who disobey Allah(swt) from among the jinn and humans are called ‘satan’ and ‘iblees’ is the title given to them. We understand from the Holy Quran that ‘iblees’ was a jinn who refused to prostrate before Adam(as). The Holy Quran says:\nوَإِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ كَانَ مِنَ الْجِنِّ\nAnd [mention] when We said to the angels, \"Prostrate to Adam,\" and they prostrated, except for Iblees. He was of the jinn.\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-50)\nIblees disobeyed Allah(swt) because he considered himself superior to Adam(as):\nقَالَ مَا مَنَعَكَ أَلَّا تَسْجُدَ إِذْ أَمَرْتُكَ\n[Allah] said, \"What prevented you from prostrating when I commanded you?\" [Satan] said, \"I am better than him. You created me from fire and created him from clay.\"\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-12 and Surah-38, Sad, Verse-76)\nNow the question arises that when Allah(swt) had actually ordered the angels to prostrate before Adam(as) as described in Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-34, why was the jinn ‘iblees’ punished for disobedience?\nThe answer is that actually both the jinn and angels were commanded to prostrate in order to establish the superiority of humans over the jinn and the angels. But only the angels were addressed because they were the superior beings. Just as when we say ‘all men’, it includes both men and women and when Allah(swt) instructs the prophets, it applies to all human beings, when the angels were commanded to prostrate, the jinn were automatically included. This form of addressing is called ‘Tagleeb’ in Arabic.\nThis is also understood from surah Al-A’raf:\nقَالَ مَا مَنَعَكَ أَلَّا تَسْجُدَ إِذْ أَمَرْتُكَ ۖ قَالَ أَنَا خَيْرٌ مِّنْهُ خَلَقْتَنِي مِن نَّارٍ وَخَلَقْتَهُ مِن طِينٍ\n[Allah] said, \"What prevented you from prostrating when I commanded you?\" [Satan] said, \"I am better than him. You created me from fire and created him from clay.\"\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-12)\nIt is understood from above that the command to prostrate was for the jinn also, be it directly or indirectly through ‘Tagleeb’. Prostrate means to bow the head, bend the upper half of the body or rest the forehead on the ground as is done in the salah. So, the meaning of prostration may be any of the above. The main idea was to show respect to Adam(as). Any action which is performed according to the command of Allah(swt) is not ‘shirk’. But Islam forbids this form of gesture. Prostration should be only in front of Allah(swt) while there are other ways of showing respect to others.\nWhen was this command to prostrate in front of Adam(as) given? It says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنِّي خَالِقٌ بَشَرًا مِّن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ ٢٨ فَإِذَا سَوَّيْتُهُ وَنَفَخْتُ فِيهِ مِن رُّوحِي فَقَعُوا لَهُ سَاجِدِينَ ٢٩﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when your Lord said to the angels, \"I will create a human being out of clay from an altered black mud. And when I have proportioned him and breathed into him of My [created] soul, then fall down to him in prostration.\"\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verses-28,29)\nWe understand from this that the command was given before the creation of Adam(as). And it says in surah Al-Baqara:\nوَإِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ\nAnd [mention] when We said to the angels, \"Prostrate before Adam\"; so they prostrated, except for Iblees.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-34)\nOne way to look at this is that when Allah(swt) created Adam(as) and brought him before the angels, all of them prostrated immediately before the command had already been issued. Or maybe after creating Adam(as), Allah(swt) repeated the command to prostrate before him. So, in both the verses there is no contradiction.\nWhen Iblees refused to prostrate and thus disobeyed Allah(swt), he incurred the wrath of Allah(swt) and He(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿قَالَ فَاخْرُجْ مِنْهَا فَإِنَّكَ رَجِيمٌ ٣٤ وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكَ اللَّعْنَةَ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ ٣٥ قَالَ رَبِّ فَأَنظِرْنِي إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ ٣٦ قَالَ فَإِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنظَرِينَ ٣٧ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الْوَقْتِ الْمَعْلُومِ ٣٨ قَالَ رَبِّ بِمَا أَغْوَيْتَنِي لَأُزَيِّنَنَّ لَهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَأُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ ٣٩ إِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ الْمُخْلَصِينَ ٤٠ قَالَ هَٰذَا صِرَاطٌ عَلَيَّ مُسْتَقِيمٌ ٤١ إِنَّ عِبَادِي لَيْسَ لَكَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطَانٌ إِلَّا مَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْغَاوِينَ ٤٢ وَإِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمَوْعِدُهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ ٤٣﴾\n[Allah] said, \"Then get out of it, for indeed, you are expelled. And indeed, upon you is the curse until the Day of Recompense.\" He said, \"My Lord, then reprieve me until the Day they are resurrected.\" [Allah] said, \"So indeed, you are of those reprieved . Until the Day of the time well-known.\" [Iblees] said, \"My Lord, because You have put me in error, I will surely make [disobedience] attractive to them on earth, and I will mislead them all. Except, among them, Your chosen servants.\" [Allah] said, \"This is a path [of return] to Me [that is] straight. Indeed, My servants - no authority will you have over them, except those who follow you of the deviators. And indeed, Hell is the promised place for them all.\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verses-34-43 and Surah-38, Sad, Verses-77-85)\nAnd moreover, Iblees led Adam(as) and Eve astray and caused them to be expelled from the paradise. This is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَإِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ أَبَىٰ ١١٦ فَقُلْنَا يَا آدَمُ إِنَّ هَٰذَا عَدُوٌّ لَّكَ وَلِزَوْجِكَ فَلَا يُخْرِجَنَّكُمَا مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ فَتَشْقَىٰ ١١٧ إِنَّ لَكَ أَلَّا تَجُوعَ فِيهَا وَلَا تَعْرَىٰ ١١٨ وَأَنَّكَ لَا تَظْمَأُ فِيهَا وَلَا تَضْحَىٰ ١١٩ فَوَسْوَسَ إِلَيْهِ الشَّيْطَانُ قَالَ يَا آدَمُ هَلْ أَدُلُّكَ عَلَىٰ شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لَّا يَبْلَىٰ ١٢٠ فَأَكَلَا مِنْهَا فَبَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْآتُهُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفَانِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِن وَرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ ۚ وَعَصَىٰ آدَمُ رَبَّهُ فَغَوَىٰ ١٢١ ثُمَّ اجْتَبَاهُ رَبُّهُ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ وَهَدَىٰ ١٢٢ قَالَ اهْبِطَا مِنْهَا جَمِيعًا ۖ بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ ۖ فَإِمَّا يَأْتِيَنَّكُم مِّنِّي هُدًى فَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ هُدَايَ فَلَا يَضِلُّ وَلَا يَشْقَىٰ ١٢٣﴾\nAnd [mention] when We said to the angels, \"Prostrate to Adam,\" and they prostrated, except Iblees; he refused. So We said, \"O Adam, indeed this is an enemy to you and to your wife. Then let him not remove you from Paradise so you would suffer. Indeed, it is [promised] for you not to be hungry therein or be unclothed. And indeed, you will not be thirsty therein or be hot from the sun.\" Then Satan whispered to him; he said, \"O Adam, shall I direct you to the tree of eternity and possession that will not deteriorate?\" And Adam and his wife ate of it, and their private parts became apparent to them, and they began to fasten over themselves from the leaves of Paradise. And Adam disobeyed his Lord and erred. Then his Lord chose him and turned to him in forgiveness and guided [him]. [Allah] said, \"Descend from Paradise - all, [your descendants] being enemies to one another. And if there should come to you guidance from Me - then whoever follows My guidance will neither go astray [in the world] nor suffer [in the Hereafter].\n(Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verses-116-123)\nSo till the Day of Resurrection, iblees is fully engaged in trying to lead men astray just as he had misled Adam(as). He employs numerous tricks for this purpose. See: ‘Satan’."],[143,"§Ibraheem(as)\nIbraheem(as) was one of the great prophets of Allah(swt). Ibraheem(as) is one of the prominent prophets who have been described in detail in the Holy Quran. There are many similarities between the last prophet Muhammad(saws) and Ibraheem(as). One was that both their tribes were idol-worshippers and the prophets actively opposed them. Secondly both the prophets suffered many trials and tribulations in the path of Allah(swt) and had to flee their homeland. Many prophets were from the tribe of Ibraheem(as) as was Muhammad(saws).\nIbraheem(as) has been mentioned in the Holy Quran. First of all he preaches to his father asking him to worship Allah(swt) and severely criticizes idol-worship:\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ صِدِّيقًا نَّبِيًّا ٤١ إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ يَا أَبَتِ لِمَ تَعْبُدُ مَا لَا يَسْمَعُ وَلَا يُبْصِرُ وَلَا يُغْنِي عَنكَ شَيْئًا ٤٢ يَا أَبَتِ إِنِّي قَدْ جَاءَنِي مِنَ الْعِلْمِ مَا لَمْ يَأْتِكَ فَاتَّبِعْنِي أَهْدِكَ صِرَاطًا سَوِيًّا ٤٣ يَا أَبَتِ لَا تَعْبُدِ الشَّيْطَانَ ۖ إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ كَانَ لِلرَّحْمَٰنِ عَصِيًّا ٤٤ يَا أَبَتِ إِنِّي أَخَافُ أَن يَمَسَّكَ عَذَابٌ مِّنَ الرَّحْمَٰنِ فَتَكُونَ لِلشَّيْطَانِ وَلِيًّا ٤٥ قَالَ أَرَاغِبٌ أَنتَ عَنْ آلِهَتِي يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ ۖ لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهِ لَأَرْجُمَنَّكَ ۖ وَاهْجُرْنِي مَلِيًّا ٤٦ قَالَ سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكَ ۖ سَأَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّي ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ بِي حَفِيًّا ٤٧ وَأَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ وَأَدْعُو رَبِّي عَسَىٰ أَلَّا أَكُونَ بِدُعَاءِ رَبِّي شَقِيًّا ٤٨ فَلَمَّا اعْتَزَلَهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ وَهَبْنَا لَهُ إِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ ۖ وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا نَبِيًّا ٤٩ وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُم مِّن رَّحْمَتِنَا وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ عَلِيًّا ٥٠﴾\nAnd mention in the Book [the story of] Abraham. Indeed, he was a man of truth and a prophet. [Mention] when he said to his father, \"O my father, why do you worship that which does not hear and does not see and will not benefit you at all? O my father, indeed there has come to me of knowledge that which has not come to you, so follow me; I will guide you to an even path. O my father, do not worship Satan. Indeed Satan has ever been, to the Most Merciful, disobedient. O my father, indeed I fear that there will touch you a punishment from the Most Merciful so you would be to Satan a companion [in Hellfire].\" [His father] said, \"Have you no desire for my gods, O Abraham? If you do not desist, I will surely stone you, so avoid me a prolonged time.\" [Abraham] said, \"Peace will be upon you. I will ask forgiveness for you of my Lord. Indeed, He is ever gracious to me. And I will leave you and those you invoke other than Allah and will invoke my Lord. I expect that I will not be in invocation to my Lord unhappy.\" So when he had left them and those they worshipped other than Allah, We gave him Isaac and Jacob, and each [of them] We made a prophet. And We gave them of Our mercy, and we made for them a reputation of high honor.\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-41-50)\nThe name of the father of Ibraheem(as) is mentioned only once in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ لِأَبِيهِ آزَرَ أَتَتَّخِذُ أَصْنَامًا آلِهَةً ۖ إِنِّي أَرَاكَ وَقَوْمَكَ فِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٧٤ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نُرِي إِبْرَاهِيمَ مَلَكُوتَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَلِيَكُونَ مِنَ الْمُوقِنِينَ ٧٥﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when Abraham said to his father Azar, \"Do you take idols as deities? Indeed, I see you and your people to be in manifest error.\" And thus did We show Abraham the realm of the heavens and the earth that he would be among the certain [in faith].\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verses-74-75)\nIbraheem(as) became aware of Allah(swt) by seeing the signs and creation of the Almighty(swt) because he saw all these with an open mind and heart unlike the people of his tribe who could be called blind for not perceiving Allah(swt) in this vast creation. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَلَمَّا جَنَّ عَلَيْهِ اللَّيْلُ رَأَىٰ كَوْكَبًا ۖ قَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّي ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَ قَالَ لَا أُحِبُّ الْآفِلِينَ ٧٦ فَلَمَّا رَأَى الْقَمَرَ بَازِغًا قَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّي ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَ قَالَ لَئِن لَّمْ يَهْدِنِي رَبِّي لَأَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الضَّالِّينَ ٧٧ فَلَمَّا رَأَى الشَّمْسَ بَازِغَةً قَالَ هَٰذَا رَبِّي هَٰذَا أَكْبَرُ ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَتْ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ إِنِّي بَرِيءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُونَ ٧٨ إِنِّي وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِيَ لِلَّذِي فَطَرَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ حَنِيفًا ۖ وَمَا أَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ ٧٩﴾\nSo when the night covered him [with darkness], he saw a star. He said, \"This is my lord.\" But when it set, he said, \"I like not those that disappear.\" And when he saw the moon rising, he said, \"This is my lord.\" But when it set, he said, \"Unless my Lord guides me, I will surely be among the people gone astray.\" And when he saw the sun rising, he said, \"This is my lord; this is greater.\" But when it set, he said, \"O my people, indeed I am free from what you associate with Allah. Indeed, I have turned my face toward He who created the heavens and the earth, inclining toward truth, and I am not of those who associate others with Allah.\"\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verses-76-79)\nIbraheem(as) incurred the wrath of the idol-worshipping people of his tribe because he rejected all their deities and declared that Allah(swt) was the One and True Lord of the worlds and invited everybody to worship Allah(swt) alone. The Holy Quran says:\nوَحَاجَّهُ قَوْمُهُ ۚ قَالَ أَتُحَاجُّونِّي فِي اللَّهِ وَقَدْ هَدَانِ ۚ وَلَا أَخَافُ مَا تُشْرِكُونَ بِهِ إِلَّا أَن يَشَاءَ رَبِّي شَيْئًا ۗ وَسِعَ رَبِّي كُلَّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا ۗ أَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُونَ\nAnd his people argued with him. He said, \"Do you argue with me concerning Allah while He has guided me? And I fear not what you associate with Him [and will not be harmed] unless my Lord should will something. My Lord encompasses all things in knowledge; then will you not remember?\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-80)\nAllah(swt) gave enough wisdom to Ibraheem(as) so that he could explain to his people that the idol-worship which they were doing was absolutely wrong and that the idols had no power to either help or harm them and in fact they could not even protect themselves. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ رُشْدَهُ مِن قَبْلُ وَكُنَّا بِهِ عَالِمِينَ ٥١ إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوْمِهِ مَا هَٰذِهِ التَّمَاثِيلُ الَّتِي أَنتُمْ لَهَا عَاكِفُونَ ٥٢ قَالُوا وَجَدْنَا آبَاءَنَا لَهَا عَابِدِينَ ٥٣ قَالَ لَقَدْ كُنتُمْ أَنتُمْ وَآبَاؤُكُمْ فِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٥٤ قَالُوا أَجِئْتَنَا بِالْحَقِّ أَمْ أَنتَ مِنَ اللَّاعِبِينَ ٥٥ قَالَ بَل رَّبُّكُمْ رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ الَّذِي فَطَرَهُنَّ وَأَنَا عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكُم مِّنَ الشَّاهِدِينَ ٥٦ وَتَاللَّهِ لَأَكِيدَنَّ أَصْنَامَكُم بَعْدَ أَن تُوَلُّوا مُدْبِرِينَ ٥٧ فَجَعَلَهُمْ جُذَاذًا إِلَّا كَبِيرًا لَّهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ إِلَيْهِ يَرْجِعُونَ ٥٨ قَالُوا مَن فَعَلَ هَٰذَا بِآلِهَتِنَا إِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ ٥٩ قَالُوا سَمِعْنَا فَتًى يَذْكُرُهُمْ يُقَالُ لَهُ إِبْرَاهِيمُ ٦٠ قَالُوا فَأْتُوا بِهِ عَلَىٰ أَعْيُنِ النَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْهَدُونَ ٦١ قَالُوا أَأَنتَ فَعَلْتَ هَٰذَا بِآلِهَتِنَا يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ ٦٢ قَالَ بَلْ فَعَلَهُ كَبِيرُهُمْ هَٰذَا فَاسْأَلُوهُمْ إِن كَانُوا يَنطِقُونَ ٦٣ فَرَجَعُوا إِلَىٰ أَنفُسِهِمْ فَقَالُوا إِنَّكُمْ أَنتُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ ٦٤﴾\nAnd We had certainly given Abraham his sound judgement before, and We were of him well-Knowing .When he said to his father and his people, \"What are these statues to which you are devoted?\" They said, \"We found our fathers worshippers of them.\" He said, \"You were certainly, you and your fathers, in manifest error.\" They said, \"Have you come to us with truth, or are you of those who jest?\" He said, \"[No], rather, your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth who created them, and I, to that, am of those who testify. And [I swear] by Allah, I will surely plan against your idols after you have turned and gone away.\" So he made them into fragments, except a large one among them, that they might return to it [and question].They said, \"Who has done this to our gods? Indeed, he is of the wrongdoers.\" They said, \"We heard a young man mention them who is called Abraham.\" They said, \"Then bring him before the eyes of the people that they may testify.\" They said, \"Have you done this to our gods, O Abraham?\" He said, \"Rather, this - the largest of them - did it, so ask them, if they should [be able to] speak.\" So they returned to [blaming] themselves and said [to each other], \"Indeed, you are the wrongdoers.\"\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verse-51-64)\nWhen Ibraheem(as) realized that the people of his tribe would not give up idol-worship, he said:\nأُفٍّ لَّكُمْ وَلِمَا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ ۖ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ\nUff to you and to what you worship instead of Allah. Then will you not use reason?\"\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verse-67)\nHearing this, the disbelievers threw him into the fire. But due to the mercy of Allah(swt) the fire did not harm him in any way and he came out of it safe and sound. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿قَالُوا حَرِّقُوهُ وَانصُرُوا آلِهَتَكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ فَاعِلِينَ ٦٨ قُلْنَا يَا نَارُ كُونِي بَرْدًا وَسَلَامًا عَلَىٰ إِبْرَاهِيمَ ٦٩﴾\nThey said, \"Burn him and support your gods - if you are to act.\" Allah said, \"O fire, be coolness and safety upon Abraham.\"\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verses-68-69)\nIn this way the fire did not burn him but by the order of Allah(swt), it became cool for Ibraheem(as). The Holy Quran also describes the argument between the king and Ibraheem(as):\nأَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِي حَاجَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ فِي رَبِّهِ أَنْ آتَاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ إِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ رَبِّيَ الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ قَالَ أَنَا أُحْيِي وَأُمِيتُ ۖ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْتِي بِالشَّمْسِ مِنَ الْمَشْرِقِ فَأْتِ بِهَا مِنَ الْمَغْرِبِ فَبُهِتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ ۗ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ\nHave you not considered the one who argued with Abraham about his Lord [merely] because Allah had given him kingship? When Abraham said, \"My Lord is the one who gives life and causes death,\" he said, \"I give life and cause death.\" Abraham said, \"Indeed, Allah brings up the sun from the east, so bring it up from the west.\" So the disbeliever was overwhelmed [by astonishment], and Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-258)\nIn this way, the Holy Quran has a detailed description of the life of Ibraheem(as) because it would be similar to that of the last prophet of the same tribe, Muhammad(saws).\nThe events in the life of Ibraheem(as) are similar to those in the life of Muhammad(saws) because the tribes of both the prophets were zealously engaged in idol-worship.\nNow let us discuss Ibraheem(as) in the light of history. The most ancient book in this regard is the Taurah. We come to know from it that Ibraheem(as) was born in the city of ‘Ur’ which is in Iraq. Some scholars say that he was not born in ‘Ur’ but in the city of ‘Kosha’ which is also in Iraq. Based on further researches, we can say that he was born in 1900 B.C. That is, he was born about four thousand years back. His tribe was engaged in idol-worship and star-worship. They would pray to the moon which was called Naanaar. They believed that the moon even had a wife called Nanjaal. Ibraheem(as) forbade his people from worshipping the idols and invited them to the worship of the One True God. The king of the land(whose name is not mentioned either in the Holy Quran or in the Sahih Hadith) was furious with him and had him thrown into the fire. But by the mercy of Allah(swt), he came out of it unscathed. But it became difficult for him to stay on in the city of Ur. So, he left for Haraan near Damascus along with his wife Sara who was also his paternal cousin. The people over there also worshipped idols but the king became a Muslim(monotheist) after listening to the sermon of Ibraheem(as). He left behind Lut(as), who was also a prophet and went away to Palestine along with his wife. There he lived in the city of ‘Shakam’ which is today known as ‘Nablus’. For many years he invited people to the path of Allah(swt). When there was a drought there, he left for Egypt along with his wife. The king of that land was very wicked. He would take away beautiful women from the people. He took away Sara and kept her in his palace. But when he approached her and tried to touch her, his hand was paralyzed. He begged Sara to pray to her Lord to cure him. But as soon as he was cured he again tried to touch her and again his hand was paralyzed. This happened three times. He finally released Sara and sent her away along with Hajira as his slave. Hajira was actually the daughter of the king of Qibt as mentioned by ‘Ibn-Hajar’. But Dabi Shaloom, the commentator of Taurah says that she was the daughter of the king of Egypt (See Arzul-Quran, p-280). This disproves that she was a slave-girl as given in the Jewish scriptures.\nThen, according to the custom of those days, Ibraheem(as) married her and Ismael(as) was born to her. In the book Genesis of the Taurah it is written:\nSo Hagar bore Abram a son, and Abram gave the name Ishmael to the son she had borne. Abram was eighty-six years old when Hagar bore him Ishmael.\n(Genesis: 16:15-16)\nThis is Ismael who was called ‘Abu-Arab’ which means ‘Father of Arabs’ and from his offspring a vast tribe spread out in the land of Arabia. The last prophet Muhammad(saws) was born in his tribe. Fourteen years after Ismael(as), Sara gave birth to Ishaq(as). From his offspring came the Bani-Israel in which many prophets were born. One reason why the Jews refused to accept Muhammad(saws) as a prophet was because he was from the descendants of Ismael(as) while they were expecting him from among the descendants of Ishaq(as).\nIt is given in the Holy Bible that Sara was very sad when Hagar gave birth to Ismael(as). So, at the behest of Sara, Ibraheem(as) left Palestine with his son Ismael and wife Hajira(Genesis, 21:9-13). The Taurah does not mention that after this, Ibraheem(as) came to Mecca with his wife and son. It mentions that he went to Moriah with his son Ishaq(as).(Genesis, 22:2)\nIt is possible that Moriah actually means the mountain ‘Marwa’ which is in Mecca. Because many changes have taken place in the Taurah down the ages, instead of Ismael(as), Ishaq(as) is used. For more information about Taurah see ‘Taurah’. In the book of Genesis, it says:\nGod was with the boy as he grew up. He lived in the desert and became an archer. While he was living in the Desert of Paran, his mother got a wife for him from Egypt.\n(Genesis, 21:20-21)\nThe Christian and Jewish scholars say that Paran is actually the desert of Sina; but they are unaware that Paran is also the name of Mecca. There is also a mountain in Mecca called Paran. We understand from this that Ibraheem(as) came to Mecca with his wife and son Ismael(as) and left them there. The Holy Quran says:\nرَّبَّنَا إِنِّي أَسْكَنتُ مِن ذُرِّيَّتِي بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِي زَرْعٍ عِندَ بَيْتِكَ الْمُحَرَّمِ رَبَّنَا لِيُقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ فَاجْعَلْ أَفْئِدَةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِي إِلَيْهِمْ وَارْزُقْهُم مِّنَ الثَّمَرَاتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُونَ\nOur Lord, I have settled some of my descendants in an uncultivated valley near Your sacred House, our Lord, that they may establish prayer. So make hearts among the people incline toward them and provide for them from the fruits that they might be grateful.\n(Quran, Surah-14, Ibraheem, Verse-37)\nIt is given in the Sahih Bukhari that when Ibraheem(as) left Hajira and his son behind, there was not a single human being there. Hajira started following him and asked him as to why he was leaving them in that rocky place where there was absolutely nobody. But Ibraheem(as) did not even glance at her and continued on his way. Then Hajira asked him, “Has your Lord ordered you to do this?” Ibraheem(as) replied, “Yes.” Then Hajira replied, “In that case our Lord will not destroy us.” Then she quietly went back to her son Ismael(as). (Sahih Bukhari: Book of Prophets, 3364)\nWhen Ibraheem(as) returned to Mecca, Ismael(as) had grown up and together they built the Holy Kaaba. The Holy Quran says:\nوَإِذْ يَرْفَعُ إِبْرَاهِيمُ الْقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ وَإِسْمَاعِيلُ رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ\nAnd [mention] when Abraham was raising the foundations of the House and [with him] Ishmael, [saying], \"Our Lord, accept [this] from us. Indeed You are the Hearing, the Knowing.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-127)\nIn the Sahih Bukhari it is described that Ismael(as) brought the stones and handed them to Ibraheem(as) who built the walls. When the height of the walls increased, Ismael(as) brought a large stone and Ibraheem(as) stood on it and continued building the walls. His footprints were imprinted on that stone and that stone is still preserved near the Kaaba. It is the ‘Maqam-e-Ibraheem.’\nReferring to this, the Holy Quran says:\nوَإِذْ جَعَلْنَا الْبَيْتَ مَثَابَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَأَمْنًا وَاتَّخِذُوا مِن مَّقَامِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ مُصَلًّى\nAnd [mention] when We made the House a place of return for the people and [a place of] security. And take, [O believers], from the standing place of Abraham a place of prayer.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-125)\nAt another place the Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيْتٍ وُضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِي بِبَكَّةَ مُبَارَكًا وَهُدًى لِّلْعَالَمِينَ ٩٦ فِيهِ آيَاتٌ بَيِّنَاتٌ مَّقَامُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ ۖ وَمَن دَخَلَهُ كَانَ آمِنًا﴾\nIndeed, the first House [of worship] established for mankind was that at Makkah - blessed and a guidance for the worlds. In it are clear signs [such as] the standing place of Abraham. And whoever enters it shall be safe.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verses-96-97)\nAllah(swt) again put Ibraheem(as) through a test. He ordered Ibraheem(as) to sacrifice his son Ismael(as) in the path of Allah(swt). This is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ١٠٠ فَبَشَّرْنَاهُ بِغُلَامٍ حَلِيمٍ ١٠١ فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعْيَ قَالَ يَا بُنَيَّ إِنِّي أَرَىٰ فِي الْمَنَامِ أَنِّي أَذْبَحُكَ فَانظُرْ مَاذَا تَرَىٰ ۚ قَالَ يَا أَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ ۖ سَتَجِدُنِي إِن شَاءَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الصَّابِرِينَ ١٠٢ فَلَمَّا أَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهُ لِلْجَبِينِ ١٠٣ وَنَادَيْنَاهُ أَن يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ ١٠٤ قَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّؤْيَا ۚ إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ ١٠٥ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلَاءُ الْمُبِينُ ١٠٦﴾\nMy Lord, grant me [a child] from among the righteous.\" So We gave him good tidings of a forbearing boy. And when he reached with him [the age of] exertion, he said, \"O my son, indeed I have seen in a dream that I [must] sacrifice you, so see what you think.\" He said, \"O my father, do as you are commanded. You will find me, if Allah wills, of the steadfast.\"And when they had both submitted and he put him down upon his forehead, We called to him, \"O Abraham, You have fulfilled the vision.\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good. Indeed, this was the clear trial.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-100-106)\nIbraheem(as) decided to sacrifice his son because he had a dream in which he saw that he was sacrificing his son and no prophet has a false dream. So, he understood it as an order from Allah(swt) to sacrifice his only son. This sacrifice was indeed a severe test for Ibraheem(as). Neither he nor his son hesitated in executing the order of Allah(swt). When Allah(swt) saw that Ibraheem(as) was getting ready to carry out his order, He replaced Ismael(as) with a sheep and thus saved Ismael(as). Muslims all over the world remember Ibraheem(as) and following the command of Allah(swt), sacrifice a goat during Bakrid.\nIt is important to make one thing clear. While describing this sacrifice, the Taurah replaces the name of Ismael with Ishaq. It is as follows:\nSome time later God tested Abraham. He said to him, “Abraham!”\n“Here I am,” he replied.\nThen God said, “Take your son, your only son, whom you love—Isaac—and go to the region of Moriah. Sacrifice him there as a burnt offering on a mountain I will show you.”\n(Genesis, 22:1-2)\nIt is clear that the writers of Taurah replaced the name of Ismael with Ishaq. How can Ishaq be the only son when Ismael was already born? In fact Ishaq was born fourteen years after Ismael. And the event of sacrifice had taken place before the birth of Ishaq.\nWe come to know that Ibraheem(as) visited Mecca two times. But it is written in some books that Ibraheem(as) came to Mecca every month to visit his wife and son on a Buraaq. One such book is ‘Taariq-e-Mecca’ by the renowned historian Fakihi who passed away in 280 A.H. But the Asnad is Hasan (See: Fathul-Bari, 6:404)\nThen, Sara, the first wife of Ibraheem(as) passed away. He buried her in the cave of Makfila at Habrun which he had bought from Hatti. After that he married a woman named ‘Keturah’ who bore him six sons (See Genesis 25:1-5). Ibraheem(as) passed away at the age of one hundred and seventy-five and was buried at Baitul-Muqaddas.\nAccording to the Taurah, when Ibraheem(as) passed away at the age of one hundred and seventy-five, he was buried in the cave of Makfila at Habrun by his sons Ismael(as) and Ishaq(as). (See Genesis 25:8-9) And Habrun is a city of Baitul-Muqaddas where the graves of all the family members of Ibraheem(as) are supposed to be present. But the scholars are of the opinion that we cannot say for certain as to which prophet is buried where except that the Holy Prophet(saws) is buried in Madina. There is a difference of opinion regarding the grave of Ibraheem(as), but it is true that it is indeed his grave. (See Fatawa Shaikul-Islam, 27:445)"],[144,"§Iddat\nThe actual meaning of ‘Iddat’ is ‘count’ but in three places in the Holy Quran it is used in the sense that when a wife gets separated from her husband, it is obligatory upon her to remain in ‘iddat’. That is, she should not remarry for a fixed number of days so that it becomes clear whether she is pregnant or not. This ‘iddat’ is of different types depending on different situations. It can be briefly explained as follows:\nIf a man divorces a woman, the proper time is when she is cleansed after her menstrual cycle as is given in surah ‘At-Talaq’:\nيَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ إِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَاءَ فَطَلِّقُوهُنَّ لِعِدَّتِهِنَّ وَأَحْصُوا الْعِدَّةَ\nO Prophet! When ye do divorce women, divorce them at their prescribed periods, and count (accurately), their prescribed periods.\n(Quran, Surah-65, At-Talaq, Verse-1)\nThe prescribed iddat period for divorced women is three menstrual cycles as given in surah Al-Baqara:\nوَالْمُطَلَّقَاتُ يَتَرَبَّصْنَ بِأَنفُسِهِنَّ ثَلَاثَةَ قُرُوءٍ ۚ وَلَا يَحِلُّ لَهُنَّ أَن يَكْتُمْنَ مَا خَلَقَ اللَّهُ فِي أَرْحَامِهِنَّ إِن كُنَّ يُؤْمِنَّ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ\nDivorced women shall wait concerning themselves for three monthly periods. Nor is it lawful for them to hide what Allah Hath created in their wombs, if they have faith in Allah and the Last Day.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-228)\nDuring the iddat period, the wife has to stay at her husband’s place so that if the husband wants to take back the wife he can do so and they can live together as man and wife.\nAs for the women who have entered menopause, the prescribed iddat is three months.\nAs for the women or rather girls who have not yet attained puberty, the iddat is three months as is described in surah ‘At-Talaq’:\nوَاللَّائِي يَئِسْنَ مِنَ الْمَحِيضِ مِن نِّسَائِكُمْ إِنِ ارْتَبْتُمْ فَعِدَّتُهُنَّ ثَلَاثَةُ أَشْهُرٍ وَاللَّائِي لَمْ يَحِضْنَ ۚ\nSuch of your women as have passed the age of monthly courses, for them the prescribed period, if ye have any doubts, is three months, and for those who have no courses (it is the same).\n(Quran, Surah-65, At-Talaq, Verse-4)\nIf a pregnant woman gets divorced, the iddat is till she delivers the child as described in surah ‘At-Talaq’:\nوَأُولَاتُ الْأَحْمَالِ أَجَلُهُنَّ أَن يَضَعْنَ حَمْلَهُنَّ\nFor those who carry (life within their wombs), their period is until they deliver their burdens.\n(Quran, Surah-65, At-Talaq, Verse-4)\nIf a woman is divorced before the consummation of marriage, there is no iddat upon her as described in surah Al-Ahzaab:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا نَكَحْتُمُ الْمُؤْمِنَاتِ ثُمَّ طَلَّقْتُمُوهُنَّ مِن قَبْلِ أَن تَمَسُّوهُنَّ فَمَا لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِنَّ مِنْ عِدَّةٍ تَعْتَدُّونَهَا ۖ فَمَتِّعُوهُنَّ وَسَرِّحُوهُنَّ سَرَاحًا جَمِيلًا\nO ye who believe! When ye marry believing women, and then divorce them before ye have touched them, no period of 'Iddat have ye to count in respect of them: so give them a present. And set them free in a handsome manner.\n(Quran, Surah-33, Al-Ahzaab, Verse-49)\nWhen the husband dies, the iddat upon the widow is four months and ten days as described in surah Al-Baqara:\nوَالَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنكُمْ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزْوَاجًا يَتَرَبَّصْنَ بِأَنفُسِهِنَّ أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وَعَشْرًا\nIf any of you die and leave widows behind, they shall wait concerning themselves four months and ten days.\n(Quran, Surah-2,Al-Baqara, Verse-234)\nAnd when the widow is pregnant, the iddat is till she delivers the child as is narrated in Sahih Hadith. It says that when a lady named Subaiya Asalmiya whose husband had died gave birth to a child two-three days later and she informed the Holy Prophet(saws) about it, he(saws) gave her permission to remarry (Bukhari, 5320).\nThe different periods of iddat as described above have to be strictly followed and only upon completion of the period can the woman remarry. During iddat the woman cannot be made to leave the house of the husband and in fact she should also be provided food, clothing and shelter during iddat.\nAfter the completion of iddat, she can take whatever she inherits and leave for her parents’ house and if she wishes she can remarry so that she can start life afresh. In this way, in Islam, whether a woman is a divorcee or a widow, she can remarry and start a new life with full dignity and without any restraints and responsibilities unlike in many other religions and societies."],[145,"§Idol-pulpits or altars\nIt is forbidden in Islam to go to the idol-pulpits or altars and offer worship or invoke or supplicate there, bow or prostrate there or make offerings or kiss the graves etc. These pulpits may either be of some idol or they may be graves where the ‘mushrik’ congregate and carry out various forms of worship. They make various offerings, supplicate to them for fulfilling their wishes etc. All these are against the basic principle of Islam, namely ‘monotheism’ or ‘Tawheed’. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْأَنصَابُ وَالْأَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَاجْتَنِبُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٩٠ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَاءَ فِي الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمْ عَن ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ وَعَنِ الصَّلَاةِ ۖ فَهَلْ أَنتُم مُّنتَهُونَ ٩١﴾\nO you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone altars [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through intoxicants and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-90-91)\nAccording to Musnad Ahmad (2:351) when this verse was revealed the Muslims started saying, “O! Our Rab! We desist.”\nSo, the people who call themselves Muslims but engage in various forms of ‘bidaat’ and ‘shirk’ have strayed far far away from Islam. They urgently need to understand the concept of ‘Tawheed’ in Islam and live strictly according to it for success in this world and the Hereafter.\nIdrees\nIdrees(as) has been described in two places in the Holy Quran. Firstly in surah Maryam:\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ إِدْرِيسَ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ صِدِّيقًا نَّبِيًّا ٥٦ وَرَفَعْنَاهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا ٥٧﴾\nAnd mention in the Book, Idrees. Indeed, he was a man of truth and a prophet. And We raised him to a high station.\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-56-57)\nSecondly in surah Al-Anbiya:\n﴿وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِدْرِيسَ وَذَا الْكِفْلِ ۖ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصَّابِرِينَ ٨٥ وَأَدْخَلْنَاهُمْ فِي رَحْمَتِنَا ۖ إِنَّهُم مِّنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ٨٦﴾\nAnd [mention] Ishmael and Idrees and Dhul-Kifl; all were of the patient. And We admitted them into Our mercy. Indeed, they were of the righteous.\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verses-85-86)\nAccording to Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, during the Meraj of the Holy Prophet(saws), he(saws) met Idrees(as) on the fourth sky. Other than this we do not know as to who he was and when he lived. What we understand from the Holy Quran is that he was popular among the Arabs and they were well aware of him. That is why nobody raised any questions about him. But the Bani-Israel had spread a lot of wrong information about him. The Holy Quran refutes the wrong things by describing him as a true prophet who was given a high rank.\nSome scholars are of the opinion that he is the same one as Enoch who is described in the Taurah:\nEnoch walked faithfully with God; then he was no more, because God took him away.\n(Bible, Genesis 5:24)\nEnoch was from the seventh race of Adam(as). He would call out only to Allah(swt) and worshipped Him only. Nuh(as) was from among his descendants.\nIn the Hebrew language, Enoch means ‘reader’. ‘Idrees’ in Arabic also means ‘instructor’. So, it is said that both are the names of the same person. But all this is guesswork and because the Holy Quran does not give more details we cannot say anything for certain. We can only say that he was a true prophet and was patient like Ishmael(as) and this quality of his should serve as an example for us."],[146,"§Ifaza\nIfaza is the tawaaf (circumambulation) of the Holy Kaaba which a Haji (Hajj pilgrim) performs on returning from Arafat and which is one of the obligatory acts of Hajj. The Hajj of a pilgrim who does not perform this tawaaf is not complete.\nRegarding this tawaaf the Holy Quran says:\nثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْيُوفُوا نُذُورَهُمْ وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ\nThen let them end their untidiness and fulfill their vows and perform Tawaf around the ancient House.\"\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-29)\nFor more information see ‘hajj’."],[147,"§Ilyas(as)\nIlyas(as) is described in two places in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِنَّ إِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٢٣ إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ١٢٤ أَتَدْعُونَ بَعْلًا وَتَذَرُونَ أَحْسَنَ الْخَالِقِينَ ١٢٥ اللَّهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ آبَائِكُمُ الْأَوَّلِينَ ١٢٦ فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَإِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُونَ ١٢٧ إِلَّا عِبَادَ اللَّهِ الْمُخْلَصِينَ ١٢٨ وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِي الْآخِرِينَ ١٢٩ سَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ إِلْ يَاسِينَ ١٣٠ إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ ١٣١ إِنَّهُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ١٣٢﴾\nAnd indeed, Elias was from among the messengers, When he said to his people, \"Will you not fear Allah? Do you call upon Ba'l and leave the best of creators - Allah, your Lord and the Lord of your first forefathers?\" And they denied him, so indeed, they will be brought [for punishment], Except the chosen servants of Allah. And We left for him [favorable mention] among later generations: \"Peace upon Elias.\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good. Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-123-132)\nAt another place:\nوَزَكَرِيَّا وَيَحْيَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰ وَإِلْيَاسَ ۖ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصَّالِحِينَ\nAnd Zechariah and John and Jesus and Elias - and all were of the righteous.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-85)\nNo mention is made of Ilyas(as) in any of the hadith; so we cannot throw much light on his life-history. The veracity of whatever we get to know from the books of history cannot be proved. So, whatever we get to know about him may or may not be true.\nWe can understand from the verse of surah Al-An’am that Ilyas(as) was from the descendants of Bani-Israel because in the preceding verse, Ishaq and Yaqub are mentioned. Then from among their descendants are mentioned Dawood, Sulaiman, Ayyub, Yusuf, Musa and Haroon. Then Zechariah, Yahya, Isa and Ilyas are mentioned.\nIn the same way in surah As-Saffat, Ilyas(as) is mentioned after Musa(as) and Haroon(as). So, some scholars are of the opinion that Ilyas(as) was from the tribe of Haroon(as). He is the same Iliyah who has been described in the Taurah. He stopped Bani-Israel from worshipping the deity Ba’al whose temple was situated to the east of Damascus and in the name of the same Ba’al, the city of ‘Ba’albek’ came into existence. But his tribe not only rejected him and his message but even tried to kill him and so he went and hid on a mountain. He prayed to Allah(swt) that the Bani-Israel should be cursed with a drought(Bible, 1 Kings 17:1-2). After three years he returned to the king whose name was ‘Ahaab’ and asked him to summon all the priests of Ba’al. Then he had them killed and then prayed to Allah(swt). Only then did the drought end and there was rain. Seeing this many people believed him and then he retired to the forests and after him Al-Yasa (Elisha) was made a prophet who is described elsewhere.\nIt appears that the Jews spread many false and wrong things about Ilyas(as) which have no basis and are in no way related to his life. The Holy Quran refutes this by describing Ilyas(as) as a true and pious prophet. But even the Muslims have imbibed some information from them. So, we should take care that we do not ascribe any wrong things to him.\nWhat can be said about Ilyas(as) is that he was born in a place called Tashini which is on the mountain Julaid situated to the west of Jordan. He was a shepherd and wore clothes made out of their wool. He spent most of his time in worshipping Allah(swt). Then Allah(swt) made him a prophet and he went with the message of Allah(swt) to the king Ahaab who was a devotee of Ba’al. What happened after that has already been described."],[148,"§Imaan\nImaan means faith and belief. Three things are compulsory for complete faith and belief:\nFirst: Whatever we believe and have faith in should also be declared orally.\nSecond: Whatever has been declared orally should also be believed whole-heartedly. Just an oral declaration is not enough.\nThird: Whatever has been declared orally and accepted whole-heartedly, should be implemented in actions; that is we should lead our lives according to the true belief and faith.\nImaan is the basic root and foundation of Islam and so is of utmost importance. Without Imaan no man can be a true Muslim. The six pillars of Imaan are briefly described below:\nThe first pillar of Imaan:\nBelieving in Allah(swt) is the first pillar of Imaan. Belief in Allah(swt) is actually found in all religions. In fact the Greek philosophers who did not believe in any religion believed in Allah(swt). Similarly the ancient tribes who had received no light of knowledge believed in Allah(swt), be it in the valleys of Sindh or be it in the deserts of Egypt. But Allah(swt) in Whom we have to believe according to Islam has three important attributes about which many of the tribes were mistaken.\nThe first attribute: It is that Allah(swt) is the Creator of this entire universe and it did not come into existence on its own. Neither does it owe its existence to some cosmic phenomenon. In fact Allah(swt) has created it according to a specific plan and He(swt) has proportioned everything in it and given it a specific task. At various places in the Holy Quran, this has been explained in great detail:\nإِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ اللَّهُ الَّذِي خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ يُغْشِي اللَّيْلَ النَّهَارَ يَطْلُبُهُ حَثِيثًا وَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ وَالنُّجُومَ مُسَخَّرَاتٍ بِأَمْرِهِ ۗ أَلَا لَهُ الْخَلْقُ وَالْأَمْرُ ۗ تَبَارَكَ اللَّهُ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِينَ\nYour Guardian-Lord is Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth in six days, and is firmly established on the throne (of authority): He draweth the night as a veil o'er the day, each seeking the other in rapid succession: He created the sun, the moon, and the stars, (all) governed by laws under His command. Is it not His to create and to govern? Blessed be Allah, the Cherisher and Sustainer of the worlds!\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-54 and Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-3 and Surah-11, Hud, Verse-7 and Surah-25, Al-Furqan, Verse-59 and Surah-57, Al-Hadeed, Verse-4)\nThe second attribute: It is that Allah(swt) has created this vast universe and is also governing it most wisely. After creating it, He(swt) has not let go of it even for a split second:\nيُدَبِّرُ الْأَمْرَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ ثُمَّ يَعْرُجُ إِلَيْهِ فِي يَوْمٍ كَانَ مِقْدَارُهُ أَلْفَ سَنَةٍ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّونَ\nHe(swt) rules (all) affairs from the heavens to the earth: in the end will (all affairs) go up to Him, on a Day, the space whereof will be (as) a thousand years of your reckoning.\n(Quran, Surah-32, As-Sajda, Verse-5)\nقُلْ مَن يَرْزُقُكُم مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ وَالْأَرْضِ أَمَّن يَمْلِكُ السَّمْعَ وَالْأَبْصَارَ وَمَن يُخْرِجُ الْحَيَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَيُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتَ مِنَ الْحَيِّ وَمَن يُدَبِّرُ الْأَمْرَ ۚ فَسَيَقُولُونَ اللَّهُ ۚ فَقُلْ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ\nSay: \"Who is it that sustains you (in life) from the sky and from the earth? or who is it that has power over hearing and sight? And who is it that brings out the living from the dead and the dead from the living? and who is it that rules and regulates all affairs?\" They will soon say, \"Allah\". Say, \"will ye not then show piety (to Him)?\"\n(Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-31)\nThe third attribute: When Allah(swt) has created this entire universe, when He(swt) is governing it and giving us our livelihood according to our needs, then He(swt) alone is worthy of worship. How can anyone else be His partner) in anything? The Holy Quran and the Holy Prophet(saws) have explained this in so many ways that no doubt should remain in our hearts and we should whole-heartedly believe that Islam with its main tenet of monotheism is the only true path and this is the path towards which all the prophets of Allah(swt) have been inviting all of us. Hence we should worship none but Allah(swt) and whatever we need, we should ask only Allah(swt) for it because Allah(swt) alone is All-Powerful and all others are powerless.\nThe second pillar of Imaan: We should believe in angels as has been mentioned in various places in the Holy Quran:\nآمَنَ الرَّسُولُ بِمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَيْهِ مِن رَّبِّهِ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ ۚ كُلٌّ آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ\nThe Messenger believeth in what hath been revealed to him from his Lord, as do the men of faith. Each one (of them) believeth in Allah, His angels, His books, and His messengers.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-285)\nIt says in surah Nisa:\nوَمَن يَكْفُرْ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلَالًا بَعِيدًا\nAny who denieth Allah, His angels, His Books, His Messengers, and the Day of Judgment, hath gone far, far astray.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-136)\nAllah(swt) has allotted different tasks to all these angels and they are engaged in doing whatever Allah(swt) commands them to do.\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ وَأَهْلِيكُمْ نَارًا وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ عَلَيْهَا مَلَائِكَةٌ غِلَاظٌ شِدَادٌ لَّا يَعْصُونَ اللَّهَ مَا أَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُونَ مَا يُؤْمَرُونَ\nO ye who believe! save yourselves and your families from a Fire whose fuel is Men and Stones, over which are (appointed) angels stern (and) severe, who flinch not (from executing) the Commands they receive from Allah, but do (precisely) what they are commanded.\n(Quran, Surah-66, At-Tahrim, Verse-6)\nThe angels follow the orders of Allah(swt) and keep the affairs of the sky and earth in order. This is described in surah Nazi’aat:\n﴿وَالنَّازِعَاتِ غَرْقًا ١ وَالنَّاشِطَاتِ نَشْطًا ٢ وَالسَّابِحَاتِ سَبْحًا ٣ فَالسَّابِقَاتِ سَبْقًا ٤ فَالْمُدَبِّرَاتِ أَمْرًا ٥﴾\nBy the (angels) who tear out (the souls of the wicked) with violence;\nBy those who gently draw out (the souls of the blessed);\nAnd by those who glide along (on errands of mercy),\nThen press forward as in a race,\nThen arrange to do (the Commands of their Lord),\n(Quran, Surah-79, An-Nazi’aat, Verses-1-5)\nIn these five verses a few of the tasks of the angels are described. Allah(swt) swears by them and says that the Day of Reckoning will surely come and what will the condition of the disbelievers be on that day?\nIt may be questioned here that when Allah(swt) is governing this universe, what does it mean when we say that the angels are keeping the affairs of the sky and earth in order? It means that while Allah(swt) is actually ruling over this vast universe, the angels are just carrying out His orders to the letter. There is absolutely no deviation in whatever is ordered by Allah(swt). Some tribes have been led astray and have started worshipping these angels in the hope that they will intercede for them on the Day of Judgement. Forbidding this, the Holy Quran says:\nوَيَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهُمْ وَلَا يَنفَعُهُمْ وَيَقُولُونَ هَٰؤُلَاءِ شُفَعَاؤُنَا عِندَ اللَّهِ ۚ قُلْ أَتُنَبِّئُونَ اللَّهَ بِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَلَا فِي الْأَرْضِ ۚ سُبْحَانَهُ وَتَعَالَىٰ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ\nThey serve, besides Allah, things that hurt them not nor profit them, and they say: \"These are our intercessors with Allah.\" Say: \"Do ye indeed inform Allah of something He knows not, in the heavens or on earth?- Glory to Him! and far is He above the partners they ascribe (to Him)!\"\n(Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-18)\nAt all times, we should worship none but Allah(swt) who is our Lord and Sustainer. He has no partners. As far as the angels are concerned, day and night they are engaged in carrying out the commands of Allah(swt). Jibrail, Michael, Israfeel etc. are some of the prominent angels who are involved in carrying out many important tasks.\nThe third pillar of Imaan: Belief in the books of Allah(swt); that is the books which have been revealed to His(swt) prophets – both conceptually and specifically.\nConceptually means believing that Allah(swt) did indeed reveal books to His(swt) chosen prophets so that mankind is rightfully guided onto the true path. Specifically means that we should believe in the books which have been mentioned and described in the Holy Quran. A brief description of the books described in the Holy Quran is given below:\nTaurah: This is the book which was revealed to Musa(as) and contains light and wisdom for the guidance of mankind:\nإِنَّا أَنزَلْنَا التَّوْرَاةَ فِيهَا هُدًى وَنُورٌ ۚ يَحْكُمُ بِهَا النَّبِيُّونَ الَّذِينَ أَسْلَمُوا لِلَّذِينَ هَادُوا وَالرَّبَّانِيُّونَ وَالْأَحْبَارُ بِمَا اسْتُحْفِظُوا مِن كِتَابِ اللَّهِ\nIt was We who revealed the law (to Moses): therein was guidance and light. By its standard have been judged the Jews, by the prophets who bowed (as in Islam) to Allah's will, by the rabbis and the doctors of law: for to them was entrusted the protection of Allah's book.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-44)\nFor more information on Taurah see ‘Taurah’.\nInjeel: This is the book which was revealed to Isa(as). Even this contains light and wisdom for the guidance of mankind and confirms the Taurah (Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-46).\nFor more information see ‘Injeel’.\nZaboor: This is the book which was revealed by Allah(swt) to His(swt) prophet Dawood(as) (Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-63). For more information see ‘Zaboor’.\nBooks given to Ibraheem(as) and Musa(as): Books were also given to Ibraheem(as) and Musa(as), which are described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿أَمْ لَمْ يُنَبَّأْ بِمَا فِي صُحُفِ مُوسَىٰ ٣٦ وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ الَّذِي وَفَّىٰ ٣٧ أَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ ٣٨ وَأَن لَّيْسَ لِلْإِنسَانِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ ٣٩ وَأَنَّ سَعْيَهُ سَوْفَ يُرَىٰ ٤٠ ثُمَّ يُجْزَاهُ الْجَزَاءَ الْأَوْفَىٰ ٤١ وَأَنَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ الْمُنتَهَىٰ ٤٢ وَأَنَّهُ هُوَ أَضْحَكَ وَأَبْكَىٰ ٤٣ وَأَنَّهُ هُوَ أَمَاتَ وَأَحْيَا ٤٤ وَأَنَّهُ خَلَقَ الزَّوْجَيْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْأُنثَىٰ ٤٥﴾\nNay, is he not acquainted with what is in the Books of Moses-\nAnd of Abraham who fulfilled his engagements?-\nNamely, that no bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another;\nThat man can have nothing but what he strives for;\nThat (the fruit of) his striving will soon come in sight:\nThen will he be rewarded with a reward complete;\nThat to thy Lord is the final Goal;\nThat it is He Who granteth Laughter and Tears;\nThat it is He Who granteth Death and Life;\nThat He did create in pairs,- male and female.\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verses-36-45)\nIt says in surah Al-A’laa:\n﴿بَلْ تُؤْثِرُونَ الْحَيَاةَ الدُّنْيَا ١٦ وَالْآخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ وَأَبْقَىٰ ١٧ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَفِي الصُّحُفِ الْأُولَىٰ ١٨ صُحُفِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَمُوسَىٰ ١٩﴾\nNay (behold), ye prefer the life of this world;\nBut the Hereafter is better and more enduring.\nAnd this is in the Books of the earliest (Revelation),-\nThe Books of Abraham and Moses.\n(Quran, Surah-87, Al-A’laa, Verses-16-19)\nThe last book of Allah(swt) – the Holy Quran: The Holy Quran confirms all the previous revealed books and presents the original and unaltered facts from the other religious books which have all undergone changes down the ages. With irrefutable and sound proofs it asserts the fact that after the revelation of this last book, all the previously revealed books are redundant because it is the original and the ultimate book of revelations which shall remain unchanged till the Last Day. Allah(swt) has promised that till the Last Day there will not be even the minutest change and the Holy Quran shall remain in its original revealed form. As the Holy Quran is comprehensive and covers all aspects of human life, no other religious book is necessary for the guidance of mankind.\nThis is what is meant by belief in the books revealed by Allah(swt). It even includes the books which have not been mentioned in the Holy Quran but were nevertheless revealed to the prophets of Allah(swt). But we cannot take the liberty of naming them because that knowledge is with Allah(swt) alone.\nThe fourth pillar of Imaan: Belief in the prophets or messengers of Allah(swt):\nThis means that we should believe that Allah(swt) sent prophets to different tribes and regions to guide mankind toward the true path of Allah(swt). Following the orders of Allah(swt), these messengers gave the people two types of instructions.\nThe first is that all the true prophets preached and practiced monotheism. If among the instructions of any of them, polytheistic teachings are found, it can be attributed to adulteration down the ages. If any messenger has advocated idol-worship instead of monotheism, worship of many self-created deities instead of the one true God Allah(swt), any form of instruction which goes against monotheism, or does not preach about Allah(swt), then that person cannot be called a prophet or messenger. This is the one supreme test with which all the prophets and messengers can be tested.\nThe second is to give instructions to the people to rid the society of all the evils and adopt an honest, upright and excellent character. And to make sure that their followers lead a God-fearing and religious life. The prominent prophets whose names have been mentioned in the Holy Quran are: Ibraheem, Ismael, Ishaq, Yaqub(as) and the prophets from among their descendants. Similarly the prophets Musa(as) and Isa(as)(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-136).\nAlso among these prophets are: Dawood, Sulaiman, Ayyub, Yusuf, Haroon, Zakariya, Yahya, Ilyas, Isaiah, Yunus, Lut(as) etc. The above mentioned prophets and others who have been mentioned in the Holy Quran whose number is 25 and the prophets who have not been mentioned in the Holy Quran are to be believed in. Not believing in even one prophet amounts to disbelieving in all the prophets. This has been severely criticized in the Holy Quran as:\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَن يُفَرِّقُوا بَيْنَ اللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَيَقُولُونَ نُؤْمِنُ بِبَعْضٍ وَنَكْفُرُ بِبَعْضٍ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَن يَتَّخِذُوا بَيْنَ ذَٰلِكَ سَبِيلًا ١٥٠ أُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْكَافِرُونَ حَقًّا ۚ وَأَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكَافِرِينَ عَذَابًا مُّهِينًا ١٥١﴾\nThose who deny Allah and His messengers, and (those who) wish to separate Allah from His messengers, saying: \"We believe in some but reject others\": And (those who) wish to take a course midway,- They are in truth (equally) unbelievers; and we have prepared for unbelievers a humiliating punishment.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verses-150-151)\nAmong these prophets, the Holy Prophet Muhammad(saws) was the last messenger who was sent as a prophet for the whole mankind.\n(See: Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-158)\nAfter him(saws) no other prophet will be sent to the earth as Allah(swt) sent him(saws) as ‘Khatimun-Nabiyyeen’ (last prophet or the seal of the prophets).\n(See: Quran, Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verse-40)\nWith the Last Prophet(saws), the religion of Islam was complete and for mankind to understand Islam completely, the Holy Prophet(saws) left behind two things namely the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith.\nThe fifth pillar of Islam: Belief in the Last Day. This is the fifth pillar of Islam. It means that there is a life after this worldly life which begins after the earthly death and on the Last Day everybody will be resurrected with this same body from their graves.\nيَوْمَ يَخْرُجُونَ مِنَ الْأَجْدَاثِ سِرَاعًا كَأَنَّهُمْ إِلَىٰ نُصُبٍ يُوفِضُونَ\nThe Day whereon they will issue from their sepulchres in sudden haste as if they were rushing to a goal-post (fixed for them),-\n(Quran, Surah-70, Al-Ma’aarij, Verse-43)\nThen everybody will be judged. The people who have believed and done good deeds will go to heaven and the disbelievers, polytheists and evil doers will go to hell. This will be the beginning of a new life which will last forever. On that day it will be said to the people of the paradise “O People of Paradise. You will live here forever and you will never die” and to the people of hell “O People of hell. You will live here forever and you will never die”. After this the Holy Prophet(saws) recited the following verse:\nوَأَنذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْحَسْرَةِ إِذْ قُضِيَ الْأَمْرُ وَهُمْ فِي غَفْلَةٍ وَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ\nBut warn them of the Day of Distress, when the matter will be determined: for (behold,) they are negligent and they do not believe!\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verse-39)\nThis was a warning to the disbelievers that after death they will be resurrected as has been mentioned in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَكَانُوا يَقُولُونَ أَئِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَعِظَامًا أَإِنَّا لَمَبْعُوثُونَ ٤٧ أَوَآبَاؤُنَا الْأَوَّلُونَ ٤٨ قُلْ إِنَّ الْأَوَّلِينَ وَالْآخِرِينَ ٤٩ لَمَجْمُوعُونَ إِلَىٰ مِيقَاتِ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُومٍ ٥٠﴾\nAnd they used to say, \"What! when we die and become dust and bones, shall we then indeed be raised up again?-\n\"(We) and our fathers of old?\"\nSay: \"Yea, those of old and those of later times,\n\"All will certainly be gathered together for the meeting appointed for a Day well-known.\n(Quran, Surah-56, Al-Waaqia, Verses-47-50)\nAt another place in the Holy Quran it says:\n﴿ق ۚ وَالْقُرْآنِ الْمَجِيدِ ١ بَلْ عَجِبُوا أَن جَاءَهُم مُّنذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَقَالَ الْكَافِرُونَ هَٰذَا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ ٢ أَإِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا ۖ ذَٰلِكَ رَجْعٌ بَعِيدٌ ٣ قَدْ عَلِمْنَا مَا تَنقُصُ الْأَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ ۖ وَعِندَنَا كِتَابٌ حَفِيظٌ ٤﴾\nQaf: By the Glorious Qur'an (Thou art Allah's Messenger). But they wonder that there has come to them a Warner from among themselves. So the Unbelievers say: \"This is a wonderful thing! \"What! When we die and become dust, (shall we live again?) That is a (sort of) return far (from our understanding).\" We already know how much of them the earth takes away: With Us is a record guarding (the full account).\n(Quran, Surah-50, Qaf, Verses-1-4)\nAmong the basic teachings of the Holy Quran is the belief in the Last Day when each and every person will be judged based on his worldly deeds so that the sinner is punished for his sins and the pious is rewarded for his good deeds. Without this there can be no distinction between good and evil in this world and as real justice does not happen in this world, the Day of Reckoning or the Last Day is necessary.\nThe sixth pillar of Imaan: Belief in destiny. This is in fact a part of the belief that Allah(swt) is the Creator of this universe. It says in the Holy Quran:\nإِنَّا كُلَّ شَيْءٍ خَلَقْنَاهُ بِقَدَرٍ\nVerily, all things have We created in proportion and measure.\n(Quran, Surah-54, Al-Qamar, Verse-49)\nTo believe in destiny it is necessary for us to believe in the following four things:\nWhatever has happened and whatever is going to happen in future, Allah(swt) has the full knowledge of it:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ\nIndeed Allah has full knowledge of all things.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-62)\nأَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ أَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا\nThat ye may know that Allah has power over all things, and that Allah comprehends, all things in (His) Knowledge.\n(Quran, Surah-65, At-Talaaq, Verse-12)\nBelieving that Allah(swt) has written the destinies of all things in ‘Lauhe Mahfooz’.\n﴿فَقَالَ الْكَافِرُونَ هَٰذَا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ ٢ أَإِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا ۖ ذَٰلِكَ رَجْعٌ بَعِيدٌ ٣ قَدْ عَلِمْنَا مَا تَنقُصُ الْأَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ ۖ وَعِندَنَا كِتَابٌ حَفِيظٌ ٤﴾\nSo the Unbelievers say: \"This is a wonderful thing! \"What! When we die and become dust, (shall we live again?) That is a (sort of) return far (from our understanding).\" We already know how much of them the earth takes away: With Us is a record guarding (the full account).\n(Quran, Surah-50, Qaf, Verses-2-4)\nSimilarly it says in Surah Yasin:\nوَكُلَّ شَيْءٍ أَحْصَيْنَاهُ فِي إِمَامٍ مُّبِينٍ\nOf all things have We taken account in a clear Book (of evidence).\n(Quran, Surah-36, Yaseen, Verse-12)\nAnd it says in surah Al-Hajj:\nأَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِي السَّمَاءِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۗ إِنَّ ذَٰلِكَ فِي كِتَابٍ ۚ إِنَّ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ يَسِيرٌ\nKnowest thou not that Allah knows all that is in heaven and on earth? Indeed it is all in a Record, and that is easy for Allah.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-70)\nIt says in surah Al-An’aam:\nوَمَا مِن دَابَّةٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَا طَائِرٍ يَطِيرُ بِجَنَاحَيْهِ إِلَّا أُمَمٌ أَمْثَالُكُم ۚ مَّا فَرَّطْنَا فِي الْكِتَابِ مِن شَيْءٍ ۚ ثُمَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ يُحْشَرُونَ\nThere is not an animal (that lives) on the earth, nor a being that flies on its wings, but (forms part of) communities like you. Nothing have we omitted from the Book, and they (all) shall be gathered to their Lord in the end.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’aam, Verse-38)\nAccording to a Sahih Hadith:\n“Fifty thousand years before the creation of the earth and skies, Allah(swt) wrote the destinies of all the creatures and His(swt) throne was on water.”\n(Sahih Muslim:2653)\nBelieving that whatever Allah(swt) wills happens and whatever He(swt) does not will does not happen in this world:\nوَمَا تَشَاءُونَ إِلَّا أَن يَشَاءَ اللَّهُ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِينَ\nBut ye shall not will except as Allah wills,- the Cherisher of the Worlds.\n(Quran, Surah-81, At-Takwir, Verse-29)\nbecause\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يَشَاءُ\nAllah carries out all that He wills.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-18)\nBelieving that Allah(swt) alone is the Creator of this entire universe:\nاللَّهُ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ ۖ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَكِيلٌ\nAllah is the Creator of all things, and He is the Guardian and Disposer of all affairs.\n(Quran, Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-62)\n﴿قَالَ أَتَعْبُدُونَ مَا تَنْحِتُونَ ٩٥ وَاللَّهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُونَ ٩٦﴾\nHe said: \"Worship ye that which ye have (yourselves) carved?\n\"But Allah has created you and your handwork!\"\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffaat, Verses-95-96)\nFour kinds of destiny or fate:\nIn the light of the Holy Quran and Sahih Hadith, destiny can be divided into four parts\nCommon destiny: This is the destiny of the whole creation which was written by the Almighty Allah(swt) fifty thousand years before the creation of the earth and the skies in ‘Lauhe Mahfooz’.\nDestiny of age: From the time of the beginning of life in the womb till the time of his death, whatever will happen to everybody has been written in ‘Lauhe Mahfooz’.\nYearly destiny: This is what is written every year during the month of Ramadan on the night of ‘Qadr’ that is the ‘Lailatul Qadr’.\nDaily destiny: This is whatever is going to happen everyday.\nEvery creature spends his life as has been destined by the All-Powerful Lord. He(swt) makes some sick and some others healthy, He(swt) makes some poor and some wealthy, He(swt) turns a pauper into a king and a king into a pauper. Every change that is happening in this world is by His(swt) order and wish. No second of the day or night is independent of His(swt) Will.\nTo believe in destiny it is necessary that we seek the help of Allah(swt) in performing good deeds and stop ourselves from committing sins and pray to Allah(swt) to guide us to the right path and prevent us from doing bad deeds because we do not know what has been ordained for us in the ‘Lauhe Mahfooz’. So, we must face our fate with courage and patience and have faith that whatever is happening is from Allah(swt) only. So, we should always be cheerful, have faith in Allah(swt), ask from Him(swt) alone and accept that we shall not get more than what we have got and in case we have not got something, then we shall not get it. Belief in destiny is in fact believing that Allah(swt) is the Creator of this entire universe and is All-Powerful. So, accepting cheerfully His(swt) decisions is the basis for believing in one’s destiny.\nSo briefly, belief in destiny means believing that whatever is happening in this world is according to whatever has been destined by Allah(swt). But we shall relate an action to its doer. That is a person who does good deeds will be called good while the one who does bad deeds will be called bad. So, a person who steals will be called a thief and punished accordingly because he had the freedom to either commit or not commit the theft."]])